{"level":30,"time":1778536917231,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LYoYkYCyGG8v4f4etiUTVf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the key context:\n\n1. **Grouping: 1.md** - This is about \"Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\"\n2. **Project**: Valley View Townhomes (SP-2025-0126C) - 39 multi-family townhome units, 8 buildings on 2.16 acres in Austin, TX\n3. **Document ID**: `1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777`\n\nLet me understand the grouping better:\n- **Topic**: Electric utility clearance requirements from Austin Energy\n- **Key Thresholds**:\n  - 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductors\n  - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral conductors\n  - 16 feet vertical clearance for driveways (parking without trucks)\n  - 18 feet vertical clearance for roads/streets with truck traffic\n  - 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors for trees\n  - 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors for trees (UCM § 1.10.10.4)\n\n- **Code References**: UCM § 1.10.0-1.10.10, ECM § 2.4.1.D, § 2.4.2.C\n\n**Applicability Check**: \nThe grouping applies IF:\n1. There are overhead electric facilities on or adjacent to the site\n2. The site plan shows buildings, structures, utilities, landscaping, or other features that might need clearance verification\n\nFrom the facts.md, I see:\n- **Easement 7 & 8 — 5' Electric Easements (×2)** - These are listed as plat-dedicated on the Mecey Subdivision\n- The site plan shows utilities, landscape, buildings, etc.\n\nSo this grouping LIKELY APPLIES to this project. I need to check the site plan sheets to confirm the presence of overhead electric facilities.\n\n\nI should review the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), building elevations, section/profile exhibits, landscape plans (Sheet 31), and the cover sheet to identify any overhead electric facilities and then systematically work through the clearance requirements against what's shown on the site plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16369,"cache_read_input_tokens":24720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16369},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26e43ce3-83cf-4ed7-a640-b8c0dd12039a","uuid":"a057c5eb-e10f-45b5-837f-6986cdcf8f9a"}
