l Construction Techniques**\n    Outlines five specific techniques for protecting tree root zones during excavation, including root cutting, mulch requirements, and vapor barriers. READ the block content for exact excavation and root protection specifications required by the City Arborist. \n\n*   **Block 2: notes — Remedial Tree Care Notes**\n    Details a six-point program for aeration and supplemental nutrients for trees impacted by construction areas. READ the block content for specific soil/foliar analysis rules, fertilization composition guidelines, and pre/post-construction treatment protocols.\n\n*   **Blocks 4 & 6: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block, landscape architect information (Blu Fish Collaborative), project location details, professional seal, sheet number (27 of 35), north arrow, and scale bar. READ for general project administrative details and use VISION to verify drawing orientation and scale.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: This section provides detailed notes on remedial tree care, specifically focusing on aeration and su\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":45}}}
