CAL., 10' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n\n## Block 18: table — Header for City of Austin Tree Preservation Calculations.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nTREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\n\n## Block 20: text_block — Project Location details.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 21: text_block — Owner details.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 22: text_block — Contact information for Blu Fish Collaborative Architecture.\n\n107 Leland Street, Suite 2\nAustin, TX 78704\nP.O. BOX 40792\nAustin, TX 78704\nPhone: (512) 388-4115\n\n## Block 24: text_block — Project Name details.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":259,"startLine":1,"totalLines":259}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778537149736,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VG2bCu9NEydnnZNATpvpcN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have the plant list. The trees being planted are:\n\nShade Trees:\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' min height\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' min height\n\nOrnamental Trees:\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 8' min height\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 10' min height\n\nThe plant list shows common names and botanical names, which is good. Now I need to check:\n\n1. Do these trees appear on the landscape plan relative to overhead electric lines?\n2. What are the mature heights of these trees according to ECM Appendix F?\n3. Are clearances documented on the plans?\n4. Are any of these utility-compatible?\n\nLet me now read through to understand what's shown on the landscape plan regarding tree locations and electric facilities. I should use vision check to see the actual layout.\n\nBut first, let me understand the mature heights according to the grouping guide:\n- The grouping mentions that ECM Appendix F contains the \"Descriptive Categories of Tree Species\" with utility-compatible designation (UC column) and mature height classifications\n\nThe key thresholds are:\n- Utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution conductors\n- Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft (prohibited unless approved)\n- Large trees (40+ ft mature height) within 25 ft\n- Trees within 50 ft of transmission conductors (non-UC prohibited, large trees prohibited)\n- Trees within 10 ft of poles\n- Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment\n\n\n- Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment\n\nThe specifications on Sheet 35 Block 11 list initial planting heights of 16' for the shade trees, but these aren't mature heights. Cedar Elm and Live Oak both mature to around 40-50 feet, making them large trees under ECM standards and potentially problematic near electrical infrastructure depending on their placement relative to conductors and equipment.\n\nTexas Mountain Laurel reaches approximately 25 feet at maturity, while Mexican Redbud ranges from 20-30 feet, so these may fall within utility-compatible parameters. I need to examine the actual landscape plan to determine tree locations relative to overhead lines and whether clearances are properly documented in the plant schedule.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4488,"cache_read_input_tokens":46948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4488},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8aec104c-0835-4d66-891b-4f34e6fe876f","uuid":"1ec80a6e-1d85-4eac-859a-18bea0170979"}
