{"level":30,"time":1778537813300,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Q8BSaVEdK6fcNGC4KudKQ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. The vision check found critical information:\n\n**OHE Line Location:** There is an overhead electric line along the **southern property boundary**.\n\n**Tree Locations Relative to OHE:**\n- A mitigation tree in the extreme southwest corner: 0 feet from OHE line (appears to be right on or at the boundary)\n- Westernmost tree in a cluster of three in southeast corner: 0.4 feet from OHE line\n- Middle mitigation tree in southeast corner: 6.2 feet from OHE line\n- Easternmost mitigation tree in southeast corner: 0.9 feet from OHE line\n\nThis is a MAJOR ISSUE. The grouping's clearance requirements are:\n- **15 lateral feet minimum** for non-utility-compatible trees from distribution lines\n- **25 lateral feet minimum** for large trees (≥40 ft mature height) from distribution lines\n\nAnd several trees are being placed within a few feet of the OHE line—in some cases essentially at 0 feet or less than 1 foot.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Identify which tree species are being placed near the OHE line\n2. Check if they are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n3. Verify their mature heights (especially to determine if they're \"large trees\" ≥40 feet)\n4. Determine if this violates EL-2.1 (non-UC trees < 15 ft) or EL-2.3 (large trees < 25 ft) or other requirements\n\nLet me check which specific trees are being planted near the OHE line. Looking at Sheet 31 block 2, I need to understand the tree symbols and see which ones are marked as 'M' (mitigation trees) in that southeast area.\n\nFrom Sheet 35, the proposed trees are:\n- **Shade Trees:** 2 Live Oak, 10 Cedar Elm\n\n\n- **Ornamental Trees:** 6 Mexican Redbud, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n- Plus shrubs and groundcovers\n\nI need to cross-reference the plant schedule to determine which species correspond to the mitigation trees positioned near the OHE lines, then assess their utility compatibility and mature heights against the clearance standards.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1973,"cache_read_input_tokens":51017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1973},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"12b946bf-9976-42c6-90c3-3d46f060701d"}
