 positioned just above the \"- OHE -\" line, visually appearing to be within 10 feet. Its canopy heavily overlaps the line."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4","uuid":"047ad960-693d-4013-bd50-679cde516320","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided landscape plan:\n\n**Overhead Electric Line Routing:**\nAn overhead electric line, labeled as **\"- OHE -\"**, is routed horizontally along the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan.\n\n**Trees Positioned Near the OHE Line:**\nThere are several tree symbols positioned in close proximity to the \"- OHE -\" line. Visually comparing the distance between the tree trunk symbols (the small circles with a cross/plus sign inside) and the \"- OHE -\" line to the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (1\" = 20'-0\"), multiple trees appear to be drawn within 10 scale feet horizontally of the line.\n\nSpecifically, these trees are located:\n\n1.  **Bottom Left:** There is a tree symbol located near the bottom left corner of the site plan, just above (north of) the \"- OHE -\" line. The canopy circle for this tree heavily overlaps the \"- OHE -\" line, and the trunk symbol appears to be visually within 10 feet of the line.\n2.  **Bottom Right Cluster:** There is a cluster of trees near the bottom right corner of the site plan, extending along the boundary.\n    *   A tree symbol located near the hexagon label **\"H7\"** has its trunk symbol positioned just above (north of) the \"- OHE -\" line, visually appearing to be within 10 feet. Its canopy overlaps the line.\n    *   Immediately to the right of the \"H7\" tree, another tree symbol (near a small **\"M\"** label) has its trunk positioned just above the \"- OHE -\" line, also visually appearing to be within 10 feet. Its canopy overlaps the line.\n    *   Further right, near the corner (adjacent to the hexagon label **\"H8\"**), a large tree symbol has its trunk posit