{"level":30,"time":1778538135139,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BsJr5fgaRy5MY9FZXdbaKZ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 36 — Biofiltration Pond Plans & Calculations\n     2→\n     3→Detailed planting plans and calculations for the biofiltration pond.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the biofiltration pond plans and calculations for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a detailed layout of the sedimentation and filtration basins, alongside extensive planting schedules and plant equivalency calculations to ensure biofiltration requirements are met.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   Scale: 1\" = 10'-0\"\n    11→*   Sedimentation Basin Area: 769 SQ. FT.\n    12→*   Sedimentation Required Plants: 77 (provides 79 1-Gallon equivalents)\n    13→*   Filtration Basin Area: 830 SQ. FT.\n    14→*   Filtration Required Plants: 166 (provides 122 1-Gallon equivalents)\n    15→*   Plant Container Sizes specified: 5 Gallon (Shrubs), 1 Gallon (Bunchgrasses), 4\" Flat (Groundcovers)\n    16→*   Maximum Spacing requirements range from 2' O.C. MAX to 12' O.C. MAX depending on basin and plant species.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 1**: drawing — Detailed plan view of the biofiltration pond.\n    21→    *   Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the Sedimentation and Filtration basins, the limits of construction (LOC), and the physical distribution of plant clusters (e.g., 6 Big Muhly Grass, 188 Obedient Plant, 42 Frogfruit).\n    22→\n    23→*   **Block 6**: table — Sedimentation Basin calculations.\n    24→    *   READ the block content for basin area (769 sq. ft.), the 0.10 calculation multiplier, required plants (77), and the provided 1-gallon equivalents by plant type (totaling 79). \n    25→\n    26→*   **Block 7**: table — Filtration Basin calculations.\n    27→    *   READ the block content for basin area (830 sq. ft.), the 0.20 calculation multiplier, required plants (166), and the provided 1-gallon equivalents by plant type (totaling 122).\n    28→\n    29→*   **Block 5**: table — Planting schedule for the Sedimentation area.\n    30→    *   READ the block content for exact quantities, minimum container sizes, and maximum spacing constraints (e.g., 2' O.C. MAX for groundcovers) for plants within the sedimentation basin.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4**: table — Planting schedule for the Filtration area.\n    33→    *   READ the block content for exact quantities, minimum container sizes, and maximum spacing constraints (e.g., 12' O.C. MAX for groundcovers) for plants within the filtration basin.\n    34→\n    35→*   **Block 2**: drawing — North arrow and graphic scale.\n    36→    *   Use VISION to confirm plan orientation and utilize the 1\" = 10' scale for measuring spatial dimensions.\n    37→\n    38→*   **Blocks 3, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative.\n    39→    *   READ the block content for basic project details, including project name (Valley View Townhomes), drawing title (Biofiltration Pond Plans & Calculations), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), date (02/13/2026), and sheet number (33 of 35).\n    40→\n    41→---\n    42→\n    43→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    44→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"bb412016-409a-4042-b7db-a32af926d485","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-36/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 36 — Biofiltration Pond Plans & Calculations\n\nDetailed planting plans and calculations for the biofiltration pond.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the biofiltration pond plans and calculations for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes a detailed layout of the sedimentation and filtration basins, alongside extensive planting schedules and plant equivalency calculations to ensure biofiltration requirements are met.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   Scale: 1\" = 10'-0\"\n*   Sedimentation Basin Area: 769 SQ. FT.\n*   Sedimentation Required Plants: 77 (provides 79 1-Gallon equivalents)\n*   Filtration Basin Area: 830 SQ. FT.\n*   Filtration Required Plants: 166 (provides 122 1-Gallon equivalents)\n*   Plant Container Sizes specified: 5 Gallon (Shrubs), 1 Gallon (Bunchgrasses), 4\" Flat (Groundcovers)\n*   Maximum Spacing requirements range from 2' O.C. MAX to 12' O.C. MAX depending on basin and plant species.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 1**: drawing — Detailed plan view of the biofiltration pond.\n    *   Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of the Sedimentation and Filtration basins, the limits of construction (LOC), and the physical distribution of plant clusters (e.g., 6 Big Muhly Grass, 188 Obedient Plant, 42 Frogfruit).\n\n*   **Block 6**: table — Sedimentation Basin calculations.\n    *   READ the block content for basin area (769 sq. ft.), the 0.10 calculation multiplier, required plants (77), and the provided 1-gallon equivalents by plant type (totaling 79). \n\n*   **Block 7**: table — Filtration Basin calculations.\n    *   READ the block content for basin area (830 sq. ft.), the 0.20 calculation multiplier, required plants (166), and the provided 1-gallon equivalents by plant type (totaling 122).\n\n*   **Block 5**: table — Planting schedule for the Sedimentation area.\n    *   READ the block content for exact quantities, minimum container sizes, and maximum spacing constraints (e.g., 2' O.C. MAX for groundcovers) for plants within the sedimentation basin.\n\n*   **Block 4**: table — Planting schedule for the Filtration area.\n    *   READ the block content for exact quantities, minimum container sizes, and maximum spacing constraints (e.g., 12' O.C. MAX for groundcovers) for plants within the filtration basin.\n\n*   **Block 2**: drawing — North arrow and graphic scale.\n    *   Use VISION to confirm plan orientation and utilize the 1\" = 10' scale for measuring spatial dimensions.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative.\n    *   READ the block content for basic project details, including project name (Valley View Townhomes), drawing title (Biofiltration Pond Plans & Calculations), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), date (02/13/2026), and sheet number (33 of 35).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
