tity, and 1-gallon equivalent for different plant types in the sedimentation basin based on a specific square footage and formula.\n    66→\n    67→SEDIMENTATION BASIN\n    68→769 SQ. FT. X 0.10 = 77 PLANTS REQUIRED\n    69→\n    70→| PLANT | SIZE | SPACING | QUANTITY | 1 GALLON EQUIVALENT |\n    71→|---|---|---|---|---|\n    72→| SHRUB | 5 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 6 | 24 |\n    73→| BUNCHGRASS | 1 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 33 | 33 |\n    74→| GROUNDCOVER | 4\" FLAT | 24\" O.C. | 88 | 22 |\n    75→| | | | TOTAL | 79 |\n    76→\n    77→## Block 9: text_block — The name of the project owner, 'WM 41 AUSTIN RE, LLC'.\n    78→\n    79→OWNER:\n    80→WM 41 AUSTIN\n    81→RE, LLC\n    82→\n    83→## Block 10: text_block — Information for the civil engineering or landscape architecture firm, including their address, phone number, and a mention of 'BLU FISH'.\n    84→\n    85→107 Leland Street, Suite 2\n    86→Austin, TX 78704\n    87→P.O. BOX 40792\n    88→Austin, TX 78704\n    89→Phone: (512) 388-4115\n    90→\n    91→## Block 12: text_block — The physical address of the project location.\n    92→\n    93→PROJECT LOCATION:\n    94→3759 VALLEY\n    95→VIEW ROAD,\n    96→AUSTIN,\n    97→TEXAS 78704\n    98→\n    99→## Block 13: text_block — The name of the project, 'VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES'.\n   100→\n   101→PROJECT NAME:\n   102→VALLEY VIEW\n   103→TOWNHOMES\n   104→\n   105→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"1f5f4078-6d6c-4b79-a620-9c12ad741277","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-36/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 36 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — A detailed plan view of the biofiltration pond, showing the layout of the sedimentation and filtration basins. Includes symbols for different plant types and specific quantities for sections like Big Muhly Grass, Gulf Muhly Grass, Dwarf Palmetto, Obedient Plant, and Frogfruit. The plan includes dimension lines and boundary limits marked 'LOC'.\n\n[Plan view drawing showing the Sedimentation Basin and Filtration Basin, with various planting areas indicated by patterns and symbols. Callouts include:\n- 4028 P\n- LOC limits of construction\n- SEDIMENTATION BASIN\n- FILTRATION BASIN\n- 6 BIG MUHLY GRASS\n- 4 GULF MUHLY GRASS\n- 3 DWARF PALMETTO\n- 42 FROGFRUIT\n- 46 OBEDIENT PLANT\n- 17 GULF MUHLY GRASS\n- 188 OBEDIENT PLANT\n- 114 FROGFRUIT\n- 32 GULF MUHLY GRASS\n- 8 DWARF PALMETTO\nVarious tree and plant symbols (PM, mb, etc.) are distributed within the basins.]\n\n## Block 2: drawing — A north arrow indicating the orientation of the plan and a graphic scale showing that 1 inch equals 10 feet.\n\nNORTH\n[North arrow graphic]\nSCALE IN FEET (1\"=10'-0\")\n0 5 10 25\n\n## Block 4: table — Table listing the planting requirements for the biofiltration pond sedimentation area, including symbol, quantity, common name, botanical name, minimum container size, and maximum spacing.\n\nPLANTING IN THE BIOFILTRATION POND - SEDIMENTATION\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. CONTAINER | MAX. SPACING |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [symbol] | 6 | DWARF PALMETTO, SABAL MINOR | 5 GALLON | 4' O.C. |\n| [symbol] | 12 | BIG MUHLY (1 gal), MUHLENBERGII LINDHEIMERII | 1 GALLON | SEE PLANS |\n| [symbol] | 21 | GULF MUHLY (1 GALLON), MUHLENBERGIA CAPILLARIS 'REGAL MIST' | 1 GALLON | 3' O.C. |\n| [symbol] | 46 | OBEDIENT PLANT, PHYSTOSTEGIA VIRGINIANA | 4\" FLAT | 2' O.C. MAX. |\n| [symbol] | 42 | FROGFRUIT, PHYLA NODIFLORA | 4\" FLAT | 2' O.C. MAX. |\n\n## Block 5: table — Table showing plant size, spacing, quantity, and 1-gallon equivalent for the filtration basin, calculated based on the area and a specific multiplier.\n\nFILTRATION BASIN\n830 SQ. FT. X 0.20 = 166 PLANTS REQUIRED\n\n| PLANT | SIZE | SPACING | QUANTITY | 1 GALLON EQUIVALENT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SHRUB | 5 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 6 | 44 |\n| BUNCHGRASS | 1 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 22 | 44 |\n| GROUNDCOVER | 4\" FLAT | 18\" O.C. | 302 | 76 |\n| | | | TOTAL | 122 |\n\n## Block 6: table — Table detailing the planting requirements for the biofiltration pond filtration area, listing symbol, quantity, common name, botanical name, minimum container size, and maximum spacing.\n\nPLANTING IN THE BIOFILTRATION POND - FILTRATION\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. CONTAINER | MAX. SPACING |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [symbol] | 11 | DWARF PALMETTO, SABAL MINOR | 5 GALLON | 4' O.C. |\n| [symbol] | 12 | BIG MUHLY (1 gal), MUHLENBERGII LINDHEIMERII | 1 GALLON | SEE PLANS |\n| [symbol] | 32 | GULF MUHLY (1 GALLON), MUHLENBERGIA CAPILLARIS 'REGAL MIST' | 1 GALLON | 3' O.C. |\n| [symbol] | 188 | OBEDIENT PLANT, PHYSTOSTEGIA VIRGINIANA | 4\" FLAT | 12' O.C. MAX. |\n| [symbol] | 114 | FROGFRUIT, PHYLA NODIFLORA | 4\" FLAT | 12' O.C. MAX. |\n\n## Block 7: table — Table outlining the plant size, spacing, quantity, and 1-gallon equivalent for different plant types in the sedimentation basin based on a specific square footage and formula.\n\nSEDIMENTATION BASIN\n769 SQ. FT. X 0.10 = 77 PLANTS REQUIRED\n\n| PLANT | SIZE | SPACING | QUANTITY | 1 GALLON EQUIVALENT |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SHRUB | 5 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 6 | 24 |\n| BUNCHGRASS | 1 GAL. | SEE PLANS | 33 | 33 |\n| GROUNDCOVER | 4\" FLAT | 24\" O.C. | 88 | 22 |\n| | | | TOTAL | 79 |\n\n## Block 9: text_block — The name of the project owner, 'WM 41 AUSTIN RE, LLC'.\n\nOWNER:\nWM 41 AUSTIN\nRE, LLC\n\n## Block 10: text_block — Information for the civil engineering or landscape architecture firm, including their address, phone number, and a mention of 'BLU FISH'.\n\n107 Leland Street, Suite 2\nAustin, TX 78704\nP.O. BOX 40792\nAustin, TX 78704\nPhone: (512) 388-4115\n\n## Block 12: text_block — The physical address of the project location.\n\nPROJECT LOCATION:\n3759 VALLEY\nVIEW ROAD,\nAUSTIN,\nTEXAS 78704\n\n## Block 13: text_block — The name of the project, 'VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES'.\n\nPROJECT NAME:\nVALLEY VIEW\nTOWNHOMES\n\n","numLines":105,"startLine":1,"totalLines":105}}}
