{"level":30,"time":1778538226406,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MzByh9bp4dwFWfcVTdo7xE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Sheet 36 covers the biofiltration pond plantings - mostly shrubs, grasses, and groundcovers (dwarf palmetto, big muhly, gulf muhly, obedient plant, frogfruit). These are small plants for the pond.\n\nThe main trees on the site are on Sheet 35 and shown on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31):\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus Crassifolia)\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus Virginiana)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis Canadensis var. Mexicana)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora Secundiflora)\n\nBut the vision check found that \"mitigation trees\" marked with 'M' are positioned very close to the OHE line. I need to understand:\n1. What are these 'M' mitigation trees on Sheet 31?\n2. Are they among the species listed in Sheet 35, or different species?\n\nLet me try another approach. Let me look for an ECM Appendix F reference document or chart that lists utility-compatible (UC) tree species so I can verify whether the proposed trees are UC or not.\n\nActually, let me search the site plan content for any references to ECM Appendix F or utility compatibility documentation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3477,"cache_read_input_tokens":53882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3477},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"f954cea0-470c-445c-991e-339b3bc6ffe8"}
