{"level":30,"time":1778538226406,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JrDuuigbL9z5DEiu9diHrX","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:110:No less than 75% of the total caliper inches of mitigation trees required must be represented by significant shade trees located in the ECM Appendix F. The remaining 25% of total caliper inches may be represented by a mixture of the ECM Appendix F tree species.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:111:All trees selected must be suitable for the environment of the immediate planting site (see ECM Appendix F for specific categorization such as tree, soil, site, or regulatory qualities). Eligible replacement tree species are listed in Environmental Criteria Manual Appendix F. The City Arborist may approve species not listed in Appendix F for mitigation credit.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:116:All trees selected must be suitable for the environment of the immediate planting site (see ECM Appendix F for specific categorization such as tree, soil, site, or regulatory qualities).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md:14:- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md:15:- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"b6d93a67-1215-4e29-a2c4-f6a45a15939e","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:110:No less than 75% of the total caliper inches of mitigation trees required must be represented by significant shade trees located in the ECM Appendix F. The remaining 25% of total caliper inches may be represented by a mixture of the ECM Appendix F tree species.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:111:All trees selected must be suitable for the environment of the immediate planting site (see ECM Appendix F for specific categorization such as tree, soil, site, or regulatory qualities). Eligible replacement tree species are listed in Environmental Criteria Manual Appendix F. The City Arborist may approve species not listed in Appendix F for mitigation credit.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/14-city-arborist-review.md:116:All trees selected must be suitable for the environment of the immediate planting site (see ECM Appendix F for specific categorization such as tree, soil, site, or regulatory qualities).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md:14:- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md:15:- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches","numLines":5}}
{"level":30,"time":1778538226406,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CxZ5Lc6QQyNHk6EHoTtiuH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The search shows references to ECM Appendix F in the context of mitigation trees, but no specific UC (utility-compatible) designation information in the site plan documents.\n\nThis means the plans do NOT include verification of whether the trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F's UC column. This could itself be a deficiency if trees are being proposed near overhead electric lines without verification of UC status.\n\nLet me focus on what I know:\n1. **Overhead Electric (OHE)** is shown on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) along the southern property boundary\n2. **Trees are planted very close to this OHE line** - some at 0 feet, some at 0.4-0.9 feet, one at 6.2 feet\n3. **The 15-foot minimum clearance** requirement for non-UC trees from distribution lines is clearly violated for any non-UC trees\n4. **The 25-foot minimum clearance** for large trees (≥40 ft mature height) is also violated\n\nThe key question is: which trees are being planted there, and are they utility-compatible?\n\nFrom the Landscape Plan plant legend (Sheet 31 Block 5):\n- SY = Street Yard Tree\n- PL = Parking Lot Tree\n- P = Parking Buffer Point Tree\n- M = Mitigation Tree\n\nThe vision check found \"M\" (mitigation) trees near the OHE line. The \"M\" trees would be the supplemental trees planted for mitigation purposes, and I need to identify their species.\n\nActually, I realize I should take a simpler approach. Let me verify the actual distances again and examine whether the plans show any calculations, clearances, or approvals related to the proximity of trees to the OHE line.\n\nLet me do another vision check specifically to see if there are any dimension callouts or clearance notes associated with the trees near the OHE line.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":976,"cache_read_input_tokens":57359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":976},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"c7821626-e2ed-4c04-a115-bdf8ad51a089"}
