{"level":30,"time":1778538226409,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W8GQdCh8kxy2EP785fTYYH","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:19:*   Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures; 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment/staging\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:31:*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:34:*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:44:- `block-13.md` — text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines a\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:47:- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:48:- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/blocks.md:37:- Various existing and proposed lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain) are indicated by different linetypes and labels (e.g., W, WW, E, SD).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/blocks.md:24:## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/blocks.md:10:- Existing infrastructure like water manholes, fire hydrants, gas meters, and utility lines (water, wastewater, electric) are indicated.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/blocks.md:20:5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:17:- Existing utilities including water lines, wastewater lines, gas meters, and electric lines.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:20:- Various easements including drainage, electric, and sidewalk easements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:22:- Notes instructing coordination with the City of Austin for the removal of power poles and electric lines.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:3:## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:5:Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:7:The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:9:The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:13:Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:3:## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:6:1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:7:2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:8:3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:9:4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:10:5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:11:6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:12:7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:13:8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:14:9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:15:10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:16:11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:18:13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:19:14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:20:15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:21:16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:23:  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:24:  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/guide.md:19:*   Spoils Notification: Must notify Development Services Dept 48 hours prior to disposing of excavated material\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/blocks.md:65:11. The contractor shall not dispose of surplus excavated material from the site without notifying the Development Services Department at (512) 974-2278 at least 48 hours prior with the location and a copy of the permit issued to receive the material.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:3:## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:6:1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:7:2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:8:3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:10:5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/blocks.md:41:Features include fire lanes, proposed fire hydrants, existing fire hydrants, concrete walls, wood fences, guardrails, sidewalks, and various easements (drainage, electric, telecommunication, water, wastewater). Property boundary lines are shown with bearings and distances. Adjacent properties and streets are labeled. Elevation contours are visible.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:3:Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:7:This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:28:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/guide.md:19:* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/blocks.md:15:*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md:18:- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-15.md:3:## notes: List of 23 standard construction notes for Austin Water, covering topics such as specifications, permits, notifications, trench safety, pressure taps, testing, materials, repairs, relocations, shop drawings, manholes, abandonments, and thrust restraint.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/blocks.md:34:d. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4","uuid":"05c11fd7-a1ee-4520-9295-10c547594a52","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:19:*   Electric Transmission Clearances: No digging/grading/trees within 25 feet of transmission structures; 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment/staging\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:31:*   **Block 16:** Electric Transmission Notes. READ for critical safety clearances, structural load requirements for roads in easements, and barricade rules required by Austin Energy.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:34:*   **Blocks 14 & 18:** Electric Notes and Austin Energy standard requirements. READ for tree pruning, easement access, and code compliance constraints.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:44:- `block-13.md` — text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines a\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:47:- `block-17.md` — text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion c\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/guide.md:48:- `block-19.md` — text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-20/blocks.md:37:- Various existing and proposed lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain) are indicated by different linetypes and labels (e.g., W, WW, E, SD).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/blocks.md:24:## Block 2: drawing — The main diagram showing the layout of the townhomes, including buildings, units, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric, storm drain), fire hydrants, cleanouts, and other site features. It includes numerous annotations and specific measurements for the utility infrastructure.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-29/blocks.md:10:- Existing infrastructure like water manholes, fire hydrants, gas meters, and utility lines (water, wastewater, electric) are indicated.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/blocks.md:20:5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:17:- Existing utilities including water lines, wastewater lines, gas meters, and electric lines.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:20:- Various easements including drainage, electric, and sidewalk easements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-08/blocks.md:22:- Notes instructing coordination with the City of Austin for the removal of power poles and electric lines.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:3:## text_block: Additional notes outlining requirements from Austin Energy regarding easements, tree work, erosion control, and safety clearances. Contains information regarding the developer's responsibility for tree pruning, erosion control, and maintaining clearances according to safety codes.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:5:Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:7:The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:9:The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-17.md:13:Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at landowner's/developer’s expense.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:3:## text_block: List of 16 notes detailing restrictions and requirements for work near electric transmission lines and easements, including clearance zones, safety meetings, access, barricades, and prohibited structures.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:6:1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:7:2. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors. Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:8:3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (ph 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:9:4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:10:5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:11:6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:12:7. For safety reasons, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:13:8. 24-hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:14:9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:15:10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:16:11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be laydown curbing.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:18:13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:19:14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:20:15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:21:16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:23:  · any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-13.md:24:  · any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/guide.md:19:*   Spoils Notification: Must notify Development Services Dept 48 hours prior to disposing of excavated material\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/blocks.md:65:11. The contractor shall not dispose of surplus excavated material from the site without notifying the Development Services Department at (512) 974-2278 at least 48 hours prior with the location and a copy of the permit issued to receive the material.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:3:## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:6:1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:7:2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:8:3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md:10:5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-10/blocks.md:41:Features include fire lanes, proposed fire hydrants, existing fire hydrants, concrete walls, wood fences, guardrails, sidewalks, and various easements (drainage, electric, telecommunication, water, wastewater). Property boundary lines are shown with bearings and distances. Adjacent properties and streets are labeled. Elevation contours are visible.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:3:Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:7:This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md:28:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md:9:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md:11:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/guide.md:19:* **Block 5**: Legend — Defines the symbols and abbreviations used throughout the site plan for pins, monuments, fences, utility lines (water, wastewater, electric), and easements. READ the block content for specific symbol definitions.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/blocks.md:15:*   **Easements:** Various easements are depicted, including drainage easements, wastewater easements, electric and telephone easements, and a greenbelt access and use easement.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/blocks.md:18:- Utility lines such as water (W), storm drain (SD), and overhead electric (OHE)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-15.md:3:## notes: List of 23 standard construction notes for Austin Water, covering topics such as specifications, permits, notifications, trench safety, pressure taps, testing, materials, repairs, relocations, shop drawings, manholes, abandonments, and thrust restraint.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/blocks.md:34:d. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.","numLines":56}}
{"level":30,"time":1778538226409,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QMUBcg8p3KMxUAze9ugygw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! I found it. Block 13 on Sheet 3 contains \"Electric Transmission Notes\" which include a reference to transmission lines. However, I notice that the 48-hour notification requirement mentioned in the grouping (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003) specifically references \"before work begins near HIGH-VOLTAGE overhead lines,\" not transmission lines specifically.\n\nLooking at Block 13, item 3 states: \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.\"\n\nThis is about transmission lines (mentioned in Block 13), NOT about distribution/overhead utility lines shown on the landscape plan (OHE).\n\nThe key distinction is:\n- Block 13 (Transmission): 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting required with Austin Energy before commencement of construction\n- The grouping requirement (EL-1.46): 48-hour notification requirement for \"work near high-voltage overhead lines\"\n\nHowever, looking more carefully at the facts.md, I don't see any transmission line easements mentioned. The easements listed are:\n- Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (no-build)\n- City of Austin Drainage Easement\n- 10' Wastewater Easement\n- 25' Drainage Easement\n- 7.5' Public Utility Easement\n- 10' Drainage Easement\n- 5' Electric Easements (×2)\n- 7.5' Public Utility Easement\n\nI don't see a transmission easement listed in facts.md.\n\nLooking at Block 13, it talks about transmission structures/lines and down guy anchors, but the landscape plan shows \"OHE\" (overhead electric distribution), not transmission lines.\n\nThe notes in Block 13 are specifically for transmission lines, and they include a 48-hour safety meeting requirement.\n\nBut Block 19 (also on Sheet 3) discusses distribution/overhead electric facilities for the project (not transmission), and it doesn't mention the 48-hour notification requirement.\n\n\nThe landscape plan shows \"OHE\" running along the southern boundary, which appears to be distribution service rather than transmission. Since the facts don't reference transmission easements, Block 19 applies to this project's overhead electric facilities. The grouping's requirement EL-1.46 mandates the 48-hour notification note referencing Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003, which should appear on the plans but doesn't seem to be in Block 19.\n\nNow I'm compiling the deficiencies across all 47 checklist items. Several items fail due to missing registered surveyor data for overhead conductor elevations, absent section exhibits showing clearance dimensions for both conductors and retaining walls, and no documented measurement methods for clearances. The mid-span clearance data from a registered surveyor is also not provided, and additional items appear incomplete.\n\nBeyond those failures, there are tree compatibility issues—Live Oak and Cedar Elm species positioned within 10 feet of overhead equipment don't meet utility standards. The plans also lack the required 48-hour notification note. A substantial portion of the remaining items cannot be verified from the available documentation, including various design specifications, utility coordination details, and compliance certifications.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5245,"cache_read_input_tokens":77332,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5245},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4"