{"level":30,"time":1778538226409,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MkC74NAWPLDjvhdubzZoLj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Notes\n     6→1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     7→2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     8→3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n     9→4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n    11→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4","uuid":"5d43f2fc-ce84-4065-95b5-bc1c4c3ca6b0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n\n## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n\nElectric Notes\n1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"level":30,"time":1778538226409,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Pe5ipXPKhgM3fBdLw993is","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have Block 19 which contains the \"Electric Notes\" for distribution facilities. Notably, it references:\n1. Austin Energy's rights to prune/remove trees\n2. Easement and access requirements\n3. Tree pruning/removal within 10 feet of overhead electric facilities centerline\n4. **Clearances required per NESC, OSHA, City of Austin rules and Texas state laws** - BUT does NOT specifically cite Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 about the 48-hour notification\n5. Relocation costs\n\nBlock 19, item 4 acknowledges clearance requirements but does NOT include the specific 48-hour notification requirement that the grouping references (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003).\n\nSo EL-1.46 is a FAIL - the required 48-hour notification note is missing.\n\nNow let me compile my complete evaluation:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY:\n\n**Grouping Applicability**: YES - The project has overhead electric distribution facilities (OHE) shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) running along the southern boundary of the site.\n\n**Infrastructure Present**:\n- Overhead electric (OHE) line running along southern boundary of site\n- 8 buildings with varying heights (33-36 feet)\n- Retaining walls up to 14 feet height\n- Driveways and parking areas\n- Landscape plantings including trees\n- Utility infrastructure (water, wastewater, storm drain)\n- No transmission lines identified\n- No gas pump canopies\n- No emergency access structures\n- No substation mentioned\n- No marquee signs\n- No decorative lighting under lines\n- No emergency access bridges\n\n**Documentation Status**:\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) clearly shows OHE line routing\n- NO surveyed overhead conductor elevation data\n- NO clearance dimension annotations\n- NO section/profile exhibits showing vertical clearances to buildings, walls, or other structures\n- NO mid-span clearance survey data\n\n\n- Plantings within the 10-foot clearance zone include incompatible species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm that will conflict with the overhead distribution line. The electric notes on Sheet 3 Block 19 fail to include the Texas Health & Safety Code 48-hour notification requirement for tree work near electric facilities.\n\n**Critical Gaps**:\nMissing surveyed conductor elevations, section exhibits with clearance dimensions, plan annotations showing measurement points, mid-span clearance verification, and incompatible tree species documentation. The 48-hour notification requirement is absent from the electric notes.\n\nNow let me prepare my findings output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1772,"cache_read_input_tokens":82577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1772},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4","uuid":"f8d13ac9-8c7f-42e0-bd28-9dde764f7ef0"}
