{"level":30,"time":1778538251194,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0183JPKmLW7uawoDLgHR564T","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet SP-2025-0126C), here are the findings regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Are any transformer pads located within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle circulation routes?**\nYes. Based on the 1\" = 20' scale provided, several rectangular boxes explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** appear to be located immediately adjacent to (and likely well within 4 feet of) the internal concrete curbs/vehicle circulation routes. Specifically:\n*   One pad is located in the upper left, adjacent to the driveway near Bldg. 1.\n*   One pad is located on the middle left, adjacent to the curved driveway between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8.\n*   One pad is located on the middle right, adjacent to the driveway/parking area near Bldg. 4.\n*   One pad is located in the lower right, adjacent to the driveway area between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7.\n\n**2. If so, are bollards shown on the plan for these transformer pads?**\nNo. Upon close inspection of the areas immediately surrounding the four labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, there are no visible symbols (such as small circles typically denoting posts) or text callouts indicating the placement of bollards to protect these pads.\n\n**3. Are bollard specifications or detail references shown on this sheet?**\nNo. A thorough review of all text on this sheet—including the specific callouts pointing to site features, the general \"Note\" (bottom left), and the \"Utility Notes\" (bottom right)—reveals no mention of the word \"bollard,\" nor are there any visible detail reference bubbles directing to bollard specifications."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":