{"level":30,"time":1778538681606,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01P6drbHfbo1Kpxr2JidT9jQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have successfully completed the structured output submission for all 15 checklist items. Let me summarize what I found:\n\n**FINDINGS SUMMARY:**\n\n**FAIL (5 items):**\n- EL-2.3: Large trees within 25 feet of distribution line\n- EL-2.10: Plant schedule lacks UC (utility-compatible) verification\n- EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans with mature height notation\n- EL-2.15: Trees within prohibited zones without Austin Energy written approval\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (7 items):**\n- EL-2.1: Trees within 15 feet - cannot verify UC status\n- EL-2.6: Pole clearances - poles not clearly shown\n- EL-2.7: Pad-mount equipment clearances - not coordinated with landscape plan\n- EL-2.8: Underground equipment clearances - not coordinated\n- EL-2.9: Root barrier requirements - zones not documented\n- EL-2.12: Clearance measurements not shown on plans\n- EL-2.13: Measurement reference points not specified\n\n**N/A (2 items):**\n- EL-2.2: Transmission lines not present\n- EL-2.4: Transmission not present\n- EL-2.5: Transmission easement not present\n\n**PASS (1 item):**\n- EL-2.14: Trees and OHE both shown on landscape plan\n\nThe critical issue is that the applicant has proposed trees (particularly large trees like Cedar Elm and Live Oak) in very close proximity to the overhead electric line (within 1 foot in some cases) without:\n1. Verifying utility-compatible status\n2. Documenting mature heights\n3. Showing clearance calculations\n4. Obtaining Austin Energy written approval for the exception\n\nThis is a significant code compliance issue that must be addressed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6048,"cache_read_input_tokens":68776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6048},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"32946716-5cf5-4f66-a2cc-5137d5435537"}
{"level":30,"time":1778538681606,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01P6drbHfbo1Kpxr2JidT9jQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping EL-MD-EXP 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nThis grouping **IS APPLICABLE** to the Valley View Townhomes project. The landscape plan clearly shows overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure along the southern property boundary, and trees are proposed in very close proximity to these facilities.\n\n### Critical Issues Identified:\n\n**Multiple trees are positioned within prohibited clearance zones:**\n- Vision analysis measured trees at **0, 0.4, 0.9, and 6.2 feet** from the OHE line\n- These distances are far below the required **15-foot minimum** for non-utility-compatible trees\n- These distances are also well below the required **25-foot minimum** for large trees (≥40 feet mature height)\n\n**Key deficiencies:**\n\n1. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)** - Large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak - typical mature height 40-50 feet) within 25 feet of distribution line, without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy approval\n\n2. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)** - Trees within prohibited clearance zones without documented written approval from Austin Energy\n\n3. **EL-2.10 (FAIL)** - Plant schedule identifies tree species but does NOT verify utility-compatible (UC) status per ECM Appendix F, which is required for trees near overhead facilities\n\n4. **EL-2.11 (FAIL)** - Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan or plant schedule with mature height specifications, making it impossible to verify clearance compliance\n\n5. **Seven items (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** - Including clearance measurements from correct reference points (outer conductor), pole/pad-mount equipment clearances, and underground equipment considerations - all lacking sufficient plan documentation for verification\n\n6. **One item (PASS)** - Trees and OHE infrastructure are both depicted on the landscape plan\n\n7. **Three items (N/A)** - Transmission-related requirements do not apply; only distribution lines are present\n\nThe primary remediation required is adding documented clearance analysis showing that trees either: (1) meet minimum distances, or (2) are verified as utility-compatible species with explicit Austin Energy written approval for any exceptions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6048,"cache_read_input_tokens":68776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6048},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","uuid":"e4670e8d-b5f3-4ecd-891e-709cd0a823a8"}
