- all lacking sufficient plan documentation for verification\n\n6. **One item (PASS)** - Trees and OHE infrastructure are both depicted on the landscape plan\n\n7. **Three items (N/A)** - Transmission-related requirements do not apply; only distribution lines are present\n\nThe primary remediation required is adding documented clearance analysis showing that trees either: (1) meet minimum distances, or (2) are verified as utility-compatible species with explicit Austin Energy written approval for any exceptions.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d74c420c-89c8-4919-b9c5-9dc6ffa1b186","total_cost_usd":0.21540040000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50104,"cache_read_input_tokens":721884,"output_tokens":16096,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50104,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":102,"outputTokens":16096,"cacheReadInputTokens":721884,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50104,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21540040000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape planting areas adjacent to overhead electric line along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple trees are positioned within 15 lateral feet of the overhead electric (OHE) line shown on the landscape plan (as close as 0 to 0.9 feet from the line). However, the plant schedule does not verify whether proposed trees are utility-compatible (UC) per ECM Appendix F. Tree species near the OHE line cannot be definitively identified, and no clearance calculations or UC status verification is documented on the plans. Cannot confirm compliance without UC designation verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan Sheet 31 identified multiple trees at 0, 0.4, 0.9, and 6.2 feet from the OHE line along the southern boundary. Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists proposed species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) but does not indicate UC status. No clearance dimensions or UC verification notes appear on either sheet.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates non-UC trees must be minimum 15 feet from distribution lines. Proposed trees are clearly within this zone, but cannot confirm non-compliance because UC status is not documented. Applicant must verify species against ECM Appendix F UC column and provide clearance calculations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are identified on the site plan. Only distribution infrastructure is evident. This item applies only when transmission lines are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure labeled as distribution on southern boundary. No transmission easements or higher-voltage facilities are documented in facts.md or visible on site plan sheets.","reasoning":"Transmission-specific requirements do not apply when only distribution facilities are present. This item is inapplicable to the project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape planting areas adjacent to overhead electric line along southern property boundary; southeast corner cluster and southwest corner area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees, which typically mature to 40-50 feet in height, are proposed on the landscape plan within 25 lateral feet (as close as 0 to 6.2 feet) of the overhead electric line. The plant schedule does not document mature height verification against ECM Appendix F requirements. Large trees proposed within restricted zone without documented clearance verification or Austin Energy approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists 10 Cedar Elm and 2 Live Oak as proposed trees. Vision analysis confirmed trees at 0, 0.4, 0.9, and 6.2 feet from OHE line. Cedar Elm and Live Oak have typical mature heights of 40-50 feet, placing them in the 'large tree' category (≥40 feet per ECM Appendix F definition for electrical purposes). No mature height verification or clearance calculations appear on landscape sheets.","reasoning":"Large trees (mature height ≥40 feet) must be minimum 25 feet from distribution conductors. Proposed Cedar Elm and Live Oak are clearly within this restricted zone at distances of 0-6.2 feet. Failure to document mature heights and clearance requirements for large trees violates UCM § 1.10.10.4.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities are present on site. This item applies only when transmission lines (60kV or higher) are present.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows only distribution-level overhead electric infrastructure. No transmission easements, transmission poles, or transmission conductor configurations are documented.","reasoning":"Transmission-specific requirements apply only when transmission facilities are present. This item is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is shown on the site plans. This item applies only when transmission easement boundaries are depicted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md identifies plat-dedicated 5-foot electric easements (Easement 7 & 8) but no transmission easement. Grading plan and site plan show no transmission easement boundaries.","reasoning":"The categorical prohibition against trees in transmission easements applies only when such easements are present. No transmission easement is shown, so this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed tree planting locations shown on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility poles are not clearly depicted on the landscape plan in relation to proposed trees. Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical infrastructure but not pole locations. Cannot verify compliance with 10-foot clearance requirement from poles without clear pole location documentation on landscape or utility plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Electrical Design) depicts underground transformers, pull boxes, and lines but shows no overhead poles. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows OHE line but does not clearly mark pole locations in relation to proposed trees.","reasoning":"Compliance with the 10-foot pole clearance requirement cannot be verified from available plans. Either the applicant must show pole locations clearly on the landscape plan with clearance dimensions, or the absence of pole markings indicates poles are not part of this electrical design (possible if service is entirely underground at this site).","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape planting areas relative to pad-mounted equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows pad-mounted transformer locations, but the landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not clearly cross-reference or overlay these equipment locations relative to proposed tree placements. Cannot verify compliance with 10-foot clearance requirement from pad-mounted equipment without clearer coordination between electrical and landscape plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical transformers and pads marked on the electrical design. Sheet 31 shows proposed trees and landscaping. However, the two plans do not provide synchronized callouts showing pad-mount locations relative to proposed trees, and no clearance dimensions from trees to equipment are provided.","reasoning":"To verify the 10-foot clearance requirement, the applicant must either: (1) show pad-mount locations clearly on the landscape plan with distance callouts, or (2) provide a cross-reference analysis. Current plans lack sufficient coordination to confirm compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape planting areas relative to underground electrical equipment locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground transformers, pull boxes, and utility routing, but the landscape plan does not provide clear cross-reference or overlay showing these equipment locations relative to proposed