ypical mature heights of 40-50 feet, are not flagged or labeled as 'large trees' on either the landscape plan or plant schedule. Mature height documentation is absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak with container specifications (100 gal, 4\" cal) but does NOT note their typical mature heights of 40-50 feet. Landscape plan shows tree symbols but no 'large tree' designation or note. Standard practice requires mature heights to be noted for trees near utility facilities.","reasoning":"Without explicit mature height notation on plans, reviewers and contractors cannot distinguish large trees from smaller species when assessing clearance requirements. Applicant must add mature height specifications to the plant schedule and/or landscape plan legend.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line clearance dimensions on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimension lines or clearance measurements are provided on the landscape plan showing distances from trees to the overhead electric line. Without dimensioning, cannot verify whether measurements originate from the correct reference point (outer conductor) versus an incorrect reference point (pole centerline). Cannot assess compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed no dimension lines or numeric clearance callouts exist on landscape plan (Sheet 31) between proposed trees and the OHE line, despite trees being positioned very close to the line (0-6.2 feet as measured by vision analysis).","reasoning":"The requirement specifies measurements must be from the outer conductor, not pole centerline (which can be 4+ feet inboard). Since no clearance dimensions are shown at all, applicant must add dimensioned clearance callouts that clearly reference the conductor location.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Tree clearance measurements on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimension lines or measurements are shown on the landscape plan documenting clearances from trees to the overhead electric line. Without dimensioning, cannot verify whether measurements (if present) are taken from tree trunk center (correct) versus tree canopy edge (incorrect). Cannot assess compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols and OHE line, but provides no dimensional callouts or notes specifying measurement reference points (trunk vs. canopy). Vision analysis found no such callouts.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates measurements from tree trunk center (planting location), not canopy edge. Without visible dimension callouts originating from tree trunk symbols, applicant must add dimensioned callouts with clear notation of reference points.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing overhead electric facilities and tree locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Both overhead electric (OHE) line and proposed trees are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31), allowing visual correlation between tree locations and utility infrastructure. Plan does not require a separate utility overlay sheet to verify spatial relationships.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) block 2 includes OHE line depicted along southern boundary with tree symbols shown throughout the plan. Vision analysis confirmed both elements are visible.","reasoning":"The requirement that 'trees be shown in relation to overhead electric facilities' is satisfied when both elements are visible on a single plan at the same scale. Applicant is not required to create separate utility reference sheets when the main landscape plan depicts both trees and OHE infrastructure.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within 15-25 feet of overhead electric line (distribution zones)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report"}],"comment":"Trees are positioned within prohibited clearance zones (0, 0.4, 0.9, and 6.2 feet from OHE line) without documented written approval from Austin Energy. The 15-foot minimum for non-utility-compatible trees and 25-foot minimum for large trees are clearly not met. No variance request, conditional use permit, or Austin Energy waiver is documented on the plans or in supplementary documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis measured trees at distances of 0, 0.4, 0.9, and 6.2 feet from the OHE line on southern boundary. Master comment report references Austin Energy design criteria and review sections (UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4) but shows no documented approval for trees in restricted zones.","reasoning":"The regulations are unambiguous: non-UC trees require 15 feet clearance, large trees require 25 feet clearance. Proposed trees are dramatically closer (within 1 foot in some cases). UCM § 1.10.10.4 specifically states variations to planting distances and utility-compatible species require explicit written approval from Austin Energy. No such approval is evident in the submitted plans or supplementary documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b13e6c9e-72ff-4936-a945-e93ae08a46d6"}
{"level":30,"time":1778538681606,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Pe5ipXPKhgM3fBdLw993is","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MWTdwLFRHNVT6tihrZarcV","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["southern portion of site near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric line (OHE) shown on Landscape Plan along southern boundary. No clearance dimension annotations or surveyed conductor elevation data provided to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from buildings. Cannot determine compliance without conductor elevation surveys.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan shows OHE line along southern site boundary. Vision check confirmed OHE routing but no clearance dimensions were shown between OHE and building footprints.","reasoning":"Without surveyed conductor elevations and explicit clearance dimensions shown on plans, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead conductors to buildings cannot be verified. The code requires maintenance of this clearance but the plans provide no documentary evidence of compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["southern portion of site where customer facilities are located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric line shown but conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) not identified and labeled on plans. No clearance dimensions shown. Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to customer facilities (buildings, parking areas).","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE line shown on Landscape Plan. Plans do not identify conductor types or provide clearance dimensions from conductors to customer facilities.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance requirement applies specifically to distribution primary and neutral conductors measured from the outside conductor. Without conductor type identification and explicit clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["building projections near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets, cross-sections, or profile views provided showing building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) relative to overhead electric line routing. Cannot verify both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building footprints shown on site plans but no elevation views provided showing projections and their relationship to OHE line. No section exhibits with clearance dimensions to projections.","reasoning":"Verification of clearances for building projections requires elevation and section views with dimension annotations from the outside conductor. These documents are absent from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings and elevated structures within potential clearance distance of OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors included on building elevation sheets. Registered surveyor data showing conductor heights and clearance dimensions not provided. Cannot demonstrate required clearances are met per UCM § 1.10.3.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets were found in the site plan set that show surveyed overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimensions. The Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground infrastructure only.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed overhead conductor elevation data on building elevation sheets. This is a mandatory documentary requirement and its absence is a deficiency regardless of actual field compliance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings, permanent structures, and building projections near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings and building projections. No clearance verification dimensions provided anywhere in the plan set.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Reviewed primary site plan (Sheet 9), landscape plan (Sheet 31), and all detail sheets. No section views with dimension lines showing clearances from conductor to building/projection edges were found.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires dimension annotations showing clearances from the outside conductor to building edges and projections. These required exhibits are missing from the submitter materials.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["perimeter fencing near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences shown on site plan but alignment relative to OHE line and clearance dimensions not provided. Cannot verify minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan shows fence symbols at property boundaries. OHE line shown along southern boundary. Vision check did not provide clear measurement of fence position relative to OHE line.","reasoning":"Without explicit clearance dimensions annotated on the fence details or site plan, compliance with the 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls proposed (Sheet 38). Wall alignment relative to OHE line location not shown with clearance dimensions. No annotated verification that minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 provides retaining wall structural details and plan view. No cross-section view shows vertical clearance relationship between wall top and OHE line conductors.","reasoning":"Clearance verification requires either plan dimensions showing horizontal distance or section/profile views showing vertical relationships. These are not provided for the retaining walls relative to the OHE line.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining walls for clearance verification. Wall Plan (Sheet 38) provides structural details but no cross-sections showing clearance relationship to OHE line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 38 wall sections show structural reinforcement, gravel backfill, and footings but do not include OHE line or conductor elevations for clearance comparison.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires dimension annotations in section views showing clearances from conductor to wall face. This required exhibit is absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Internal driveways shown on site plan and grading plan. No vertical clearance dimensions shown between finished driveway grade elevations and overhead electric line. No mid-span clearance survey data provided. Cannot verify 16-foot minimum vertical clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (areas with truck traffic) from lowest point of OHE.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading Plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway grades and contours. Landscape Plan shows OHE line routing. No cross-sections or profiles show vertical relationships between driveway grades and OHE line heights.","reasoning":"Vertical clearance verification requires either engineer-calculated clearances or registered surveyor mid-span clearance data. Neither is provided in the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["throughout site where OHE line exists"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets between the OHE line and any site features. When clearances must be shown, plans do not indicate whether dimensions are measured from the outside conductor (as required) or from pole centerline/other reference. Measurement methodology cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of all sheets (site plan, landscape plan, grading plan, electrical plan, utility plans) found no clearance dimension annotations shown anywhere on the plans.","reasoning":"The code requires that clearances be measured from the outside conductor (not pole center), and dimension lines must show this measurement method. Complete absence of clearance dimensions means this requirement cannot be met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["driveways and areas where vertical clearances may be marginal"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data provided. Building heights (up to 36 feet) and driveway grades shown but without surveyed overhead line heights and mid-span clearance verification. Required to demonstrate existing overhead facilities meet minimum vertical clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading Plan provides finished floor elevations (FFE) and site benchmarks (BM #1 = 678.52', BM #2 = 681.08'). No OHE conductor height data provided; no surveyor mid-span measurements documented.","reasoning":"When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or unverifiable from plan geometry alone, UCM § 1.10.3 requires registered surveyor field measurements and documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape planting areas along southern boundary near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows multiple trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm as shade trees. Live Oak and Cedar Elm are NOT utility-compatible species (mature heights >40 feet, not on ECM Appendix F utility-compatible list). Vision check confirmed trees positioned within 10 feet of OHE line with canopy overlap. Only Texas Mountain Laurel (2) and Mexican Redbud (6) are utility-compatible alternatives shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Landscape Plan confirmed trees within 10 feet of OHE line at multiple locations. Plant list shows: 10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak (not utility-compatible); 2 Texas Mountain Laurel, 6 Mexican Redbud (utility-compatible). Large oaks and elms have canopies shown overlapping OHE line.","reasoning":"ECM and UCM standards limit trees within 10 feet of distribution conductors to utility-compatible species (generally ≤20 feet mature height). Live Oaks and Cedar Elms grow 40-50 feet and are not on the utility-compatible list. Their placement within 10 feet violates tree clearance requirements.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["entire site construction area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. Sheet 3 Block 19 (Electric Notes) lists Austin Energy requirements but does not include this mandatory 48-hour notification requirement. Note must be added to cover sheet or general notes.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Block 19 (Electric Notes) was reviewed and contains 5 items regarding tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs. No item references the Texas Health & Safety Code 48-hour notification requirement to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 require a plan note mandating 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before construction work near high-voltage overhead lines. This is a mandatory contractual requirement and its absence from the plans is a deficiency.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Gas pump canopies not proposed. Project is multi-family residential (39 townhome units); no fuel service infrastructure included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows only residential townhome buildings, no gas pumps or fuel service stations.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when gas pump canopies are proposed. No such facilities exist in this project scope.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Stairs, elevated walkways, and elevated platforms not shown as separate structures. Accessible routes and pedestrian pathways shown as ground-level features only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows sidewalks and pedestrian pathways at ground level. No elevated platforms, elevated walkways, or raised structures independent of buildings are proposed.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when such structures are proposed and overhead electric facilities exist. No elevated features that would trigger this requirement are shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings adjacent to Valley View Road right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings proposed adjacent to Valley View Road. OHE line shown on landscape plan but its precise location relative to ROW and whether electric facilities exist/will be relocated in ROW not clearly documented. No utility plan showing AE facilities in ROW. Clearance verification cannot be completed without utility plan data.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows Valley View Road to the west of property. Landscape plan shows OHE line on site but not clearly related to ROW. No separate utility/ROW coordination plan provided.","reasoning":"Verification requires utility plan showing overhead electric facility locations in the adjacent ROW and clearance dimensions from buildings. These specific exhibits are not in the provided plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["perimeter fencing and electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles shown on survey (Sheet 4). Perimeter fences shown on landscape plan. Fence post locations relative to existing poles not clearly annotated with 10-foot clearance dimensions. Pole location precision not sufficient to verify 10-foot separation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles marked as symbols. Landscape Plan shows fence alignments. No dimension annotations showing pole-to-fence-post distances.","reasoning":"Clearance verification requires specific dimension annotations from fence post centers to pole centers. Without such annotations, the 10-foot minimum separation cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation shown on plans. Requirement applies only when fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with existing substation fences.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md and all site plan sheets found no substation facilities mentioned or depicted.","reasoning":"Substation requirement does not apply to this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) identified on project. OHE shown is distribution voltage (typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV). Transmission facility requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md contains no reference to transmission lines or 60kV+ facilities. Landscape plan labels line as OHE (overhead electric), which is distribution. Sheet 3 Block 13 discusses transmission if any exists, but no transmission easements are recorded for this site.","reasoning":"Transmission fencing requirements apply only to transmission-voltage facilities (≥60kV). This project has distribution voltage only.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["vehicle barrier fencing near OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing specifically identified. Standard perimeter fencing shown on landscape plan. Cannot determine if any fencing beneath or adjacent to OHE line is vehicle barrier type or if clearance verification exhibits exist.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows fencing symbols but does not distinguish vehicle barriers from other fence types. No section exhibits provided showing clearance verification for any fence type beneath OHE line.","reasoning":"Without specific identification of vehicle barrier fencing and corresponding section exhibits with clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation adjacent to site. Requirement applies only to retaining walls proposed adjacent to substation property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No substation shown on plans or mentioned in facts.","reasoning":"Substation separation requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms proposed. Structures shown are standard townhome buildings and site amenities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building layouts are ground-level or conventional multi-story residential structures. No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to emergency access structures. None are proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["vehicle parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Parking areas shown on site plan. No vertical clearance verification dimensions shown between parking grade elevations and OHE line. No note confirming clearance requirement compliance or specifying required clearance value.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking areas (10 surface, 78 garage spaces). Grading plan shows parking lot elevations. No section views showing relationship between parking surface elevation and OHE line height.","reasoning":"Vertical clearance verification for parking areas requires dimension annotations or section views. Neither is provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines present. OHE shown is distribution voltage. Transmission vertical clearance requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts and plans show no transmission facilities on or adjacent to site.","reasoning":"Transmission clearance requirements apply only to transmission voltage (≥60kV) facilities.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Valley View Road is classified as Level 1 (Local Street), not highway or freeway. No transmission structures with underbuilt distribution. Requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md shows Valley View Road as ASMP Street Level 1 - Local Street. No transmission structures identified.","reasoning":"Highway/freeway distribution underbuilt requirement applies only to those roadway types with transmission structures.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["driveways where existing poles may conflict"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles shown on survey (Sheet 4). Proposed driveways shown on site plan. Pole-to-driveway relationships not clearly annotated with dimensions or relocation notes. Cannot determine if poles are in conflict or have been relocated 30 feet minimum.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey shows pole symbols. Site plan shows driveway alignments. No dimension annotations showing pole offset from driveways, and no relocation notes provided.","reasoning":"Verification requires either dimension annotations showing >30-foot clearance or relocation notes. Without these, conflict status cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles proposed under overhead electric lines. Street lighting not shown on photometric plan or site plan as new installations under OHE routing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and photometric/lighting plan reviewed. No new streetlight poles shown beneath OHE line routing.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when new streetlights under overhead lines are proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["sidewalks at property boundaries along ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks proposed along Valley View Road frontage. Existing power poles shown on survey (Sheet 4). Sidewalk alignment at property corners relative to pole locations not clearly dimensioned or noted. Cannot verify clearance from sidewalk edges.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey shows existing poles. Landscape plan shows sidewalk routing along property boundary. No dimension annotations showing sidewalk edge-to-pole clearances at property limits.","reasoning":"Verification requires specific dimensions showing sidewalk cleared from poles at each property end.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["trash collection areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash collection area locations shown on site plan. Cannot determine from plans if trash enclosures or receptacles are positioned beneath OHE line or within clearance zone. No dimension annotations or notes addressing trash bin height during service relative to OHE line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows trash collection areas labeled. OHE line location on landscape plan. No section view showing relationship between trash bin locations and OHE line height.","reasoning":"Verification requires specific location coordinates and height analysis of raised bins during service. These details are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plantings along southern boundary beneath OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows tree canopies overlapping the OHE line routing along southern boundary. Trees with large canopy spreads (Live Oak, Cedar Elm) are positioned directly beneath or over the overhead conductor. UCM § 1.10.3 prohibits customer facilities (including vegetation) from being installed under or over overhead distribution facilities, separate from clearance distance requirements. This absolute prohibition is violated by tree placement shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed multiple trees on landscape plan positioned with canopies overlapping the OHE line path. Plant list includes large tree species (Oak, Elm) unsuitable for positions under overhead lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 contains an absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities under or over overhead distribution facilities, distinct from maintaining clearance distances. Tree canopies shown overlapping the conductor violate this prohibition.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water service lines shown on utility plans. Water meter locations not explicitly dimensioned or located on utility plan relative to any overhead electric service-drop conductor routing. No clearance verification dimensions provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 20) shows water main connections. Electric Meter/Service Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electric infrastructure. Water meter specific locations relative to overhead service drops not clearly documented.","reasoning":"Verification requires specific meter location coordinates and clearance dimensions from overhead conductors. These are not annotated on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["water utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines proposed within site. No clearance dimensions shown between water line routing and overhead electric distribution facilities. Plan does not demonstrate compliance with clearance requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan sheets show water line routing but no dimension annotations showing clearances from overhead facilities. OHE shown on separate landscape plan.","reasoning":"Clearance verification requires specific dimension annotations showing utility-to-conductor relationships. These are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["building foundations near property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building setbacks from property lines shown on site plan. No specific analysis or notation regarding foundation location clearance from property line to allow space for electric facility installation/maintenance within adjacent ROW.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building locations and property boundaries. No specific dimension annotations or note addressing foundation-to-property-line clearances for utility access.","reasoning":"Verification requires specific documentation showing 5-foot minimum clearance from property line for electric facility work areas.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines crossing proposed or existing roadways. OHE line shown runs along property boundary parallel to roadway, not across it.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows OHE line routing along southern boundary of site. No overhead lines shown crossing roads or driveways at angle other than parallel.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when new overhead lines cross roadways. No such design is shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No secondary and primary overhead lines shown crossing over one another. Electrical Design Plan shows underground infrastructure only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure. No secondary line crossings over primary lines evident.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only to overhead line designs with crossing secondary/primary arrangements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs proposed. Site has standard residential townhome architecture without decorative signage features.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevations and site plans show no marquee or canopy signs.","reasoning":"Marquee sign clearance requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion. Project design shows conversion to full underground distribution without new pole installation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground infrastructure. No new above-ground power poles indicated.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when new poles are proposed for underground conversion.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No decorative lighting fixtures proposed under overhead electric lines. Landscape plan shows standard site lighting with no decorative fixtures beneath OHE routing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan does not show decorative lighting features positioned beneath OHE line.","reasoning":"Requirement applies only when decorative lighting under overhead lines is proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads and pull boxes but meter locations not clearly identified with surrounding features or obstructions. Cannot verify whether proposed meter locations have 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom working clearances required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical infrastructure but meter access details and working clearance dimensions not provided. No enlarged meter area details showing obstruction-free zones.","reasoning":"Verification requires enlarged detail sheets showing meter locations with surrounding features (walls, fences, landscaping) and dimension annotations confirming required working clearances.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["buildings near existing streetlight poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing streetlight poles shown on survey (Sheet 4). Building locations shown on site plan. Clearance dimensions between buildings and streetlight pole locations not annotated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey shows existing street-side poles. Site plan shows building positions relative to property boundaries and ROW. No specific clearance annotations.","reasoning":"Verification requires dimension annotations showing building clearances from existing streetlight poles.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["driveways and accessible paths near existing poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing utility poles shown on survey. Down guy wire locations not indicated on plans. Proposed driveways and accessible paths shown on site plan. Conflicts between down guy wires and proposed site features not documented or resolved. Cannot verify whether down guys have been addressed through pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey shows pole symbols but down guy anchor points are typically not clearly marked. Site plan shows driveway and path routing. No note addressing down guy conflict resolution.","reasoning":"Down guys are frequently omitted from plans but are real infrastructure that must be addressed when site design conflicts exist. Cannot confirm resolution without explicit documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled transmission guy anchors from transmission structures. OHE is distribution voltage; transmission guy easements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission structures identified on plans or in facts.","reasoning":"Angled transmission guy easement requirements apply only to transmission-voltage facilities.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["distribution poles with down guy anchors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing utility poles shown on survey. Down guy anchor locations and associated easements not documented on Plat (Sheet 2) or other drawings. Cannot verify 10-foot-wide by 5-foot-extension easements are shown for down guy anchors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey shows pole locations but down guy details are rarely visible on survey documents. Plat sheet does not show down guy easement boundaries.","reasoning":"Down guy anchor easements must be documented on the plat if they exist on site. Absence of this documentation creates uncertainty.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["pad-mounted transformers"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted transformers shown on Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21). No vertical clearance dimension from transformer equipment top to OHE line conductors shown. Cannot verify minimum 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance above transformer equipment.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations on the site plan. No section view or vertical clearance dimension provided showing transformer height and clearance to OHE line.","reasoning":"Verification requires section view with dimension showing vertical distance from transformer top to conductor.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers are pad-mounted configurations, not in covered niches or recessed installations. Niche service configuration clearance requirement (35-foot vertical niche clearance) does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical Design Plan shows pad-mounted transformers in open outdoor configuration.","reasoning":"The 35-foot niche clearance requirement applies only to transformers in covered or recessed niche configurations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["construction staging and equipment zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment operation zones not shown on site plan or construction logistics plan. OSHA 10-foot radial clearance requirement from energized overhead lines during construction not documented or noted. Cannot verify construction activities will maintain required clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No construction logistics or phasing plan provided. Site plan does not show designated staging areas, crane swing zones, or material storage areas with reference to OHE line location.","reasoning":"Verification requires construction logistics plan with clearance annotations. This document is not in the submitted set.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["service-mast installations through roofs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations shown on building elevation sheets. Building elevations do not detail service entry method or roof clearance for service equipment. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if within 4 feet of roof edge) per UCM § 1.10.6.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets provided. Site plan and electrical plan do not show proposed service-mast or roof-penetration details.","reasoning":"Verification requires building elevation sheets showing service entry details and roof clearance dimensions.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1772,"cache_read_input_tokens":82577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1772},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cf9b9a6-a069-491a-8521-ba77a83a73f4","uuid":"a77a24ac-326a-4a61-b0d9-f410fa2ef9b7"}
