{"level":30,"time":1778539022500,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyBPwmJfBJEdTsDz7w536y","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of Sheet 21 (\"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"):\n\n**Yes, easements are explicitly shown on this sheet.** The plan includes dashed lines denoting various easements, with specific labels such as:\n*   \"25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2011021707...\" (along the eastern/right boundary)\n*   \"Wastewater Easement Doc#...\" (near the northwest corner)\n*   \"5' P.U.E.\" (near the northern boundary)\n*   \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"Elec. Easement...\" (along the southern boundary)\n*   \"Sidewalk Easement...\" (along the western street frontage)\n\n**Yes, there are transformer pads located within these easement areas.** Specifically:\n1.  On the center-right side of the plan, located east of the area between Building 4 and Building 5, there is a square box with a leader line labeling it as an **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. This pad is drawn within the dashed boundary lines denoting the **\"25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2011021707...\"**.\n2.  Further south along that same eastern boundary (situated east of Building 7 and south of Building 6), there is another **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** that is drawn within the overlapping dashed easement boundaries labeled **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** and **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\"**."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85cce1e8-6e77-4208-9a6d-06fe1aa951a1","uuid":"f66a2784-c565-4cd1-849b-4085cae47532","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of Sheet 21 (\"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"):\n\n**Yes, easements are explicitly shown on this sheet.** The plan includes dashed lines denoting various easements, with specific labels such as:\n*   \"25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2011021707...\" (along the eastern/right boundary)\n*   \"Wastewater Easement Doc#...\" (near the northwest corner)\n*   \"5' P.U.E.\" (near the northern boundary)\n*   \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\" (along the eastern boundary)\n*   \"Elec. Easement...\" (along the southern boundary)\n*   \"Sidewalk Easement...\" (along the western street frontage)\n\n**Yes, there are transformer pads located within these easement areas.** Specifically:\n1.  On the center-right side of the plan, located east of the area between Building 4 and Building 5, there is a square box with a leader line labeling it as an **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. This pad is drawn within the dashed boundary lines denoting the **\"25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2011021707...\"**.\n2.  Further south along that same eastern boundary (situated east of Building 7 and south of Building 6), there is another **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** that is drawn within the overlapping dashed easement boundaries labeled **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** and **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\"**."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778539023088,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01S8QatDjHmBkwmUSqfpUgkb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! So I found that Sheet 3 has electric transmission notes with a 48-hour notification requirement, but it's specifically about a \"pre-construction safety meeting\" with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. This is different from the UCM § 1.10.2 requirement which is about notifying Austin Energy \"at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines\" per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752.\n\nThe note found is about TRANSMISSION lines specifically (requiring 20-foot clearance), not distribution lines. The checklist item EL-1.46 is broader - it applies when ANY high-voltage overhead lines exist.\n\nLet me read the blocks files for Sheet 3 to see the full text of the electric transmission notes and any other electric-related notes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2732,"cache_read_input_tokens":62190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2732},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26e43ce3-83cf-4ed7-a640-b8c0dd12039a","uuid":"e57e75e7-5b24-4e46-8088-7f3416b0fc2b"}
{"level":30,"time":1778539023362,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PgfV7X7WWxvT77QwqjmgmS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - I've confirmed that there are three proposed trees within 10 feet of the OHE line, but their species are not specifically labeled on the landscape plan. The trees are marked as M (mitigation) or P (parking buffer point), but no species identification or utility-compatible marking is shown.\n\nNow I need to find the plant list to see if there's species information there. Let me check Sheet 32 or 35 which are the tree list sheets.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2190,"cache_read_input_tokens":67279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2190},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63269730-a4a1-4a44-9c02-2ba8ff960fa8","uuid":"e0ab0855-f48a-44ac-8af9-452473ae3b40"}
