ts (drainage, electric, telecommunication, water, wastewater). Property boundary lines are shown with bearings and distances. Adjacent properties and streets are labeled. Elevation contours are visible.\n\n## Block 3: notes — The block provides information on two benchmarks, including their location, elevation, and datum.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 4: notes — The block contains a brief note directing the reader to the landscape plan for the tree list.\n\nTree List\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n## Block 5: notes — The block contains a numbered list of Fire Zone Notes, specifying requirements for signage, painting, underground mains, and private hydrants.\n\nFire Zone Notes\n1. Restricted Zone signage to be placed on front of lockers and along boat slip retaining walls as necessary or\nrequired.\n2. Stencil the words \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" in white letters at least 4\" high at 30 foot intervals along the\ncurb and the entire curb shall be painted red to serve as the background for the white letters.\n3. Signs stating \"FIRE ZONE/ TOW-AWAY ZONE\" shall be posted at both ends of a fire zone and at each entry\nand exit point which constitutes a portion of the fire zone or fire lane. Signs shall comply with Standard City of\nAustin Detail 901S-6.\n4. Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the\nFire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at\none time, unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\n5. All private hydrants shall be painted red.\n\n## Block 6: notes — The block contains the legal description of the property.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 7: notes — The 