{"level":30,"time":1778539091457,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NgQLddC5NCJh3ePhgfnSHZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Sheet 35 has plant schedules that list the shade trees. The key points are:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.)\n- 2 Live Oak (100 gal.)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n\nNow I need to check if these species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. The grouping mentions ECM Appendix F \"Descriptive Categories of Tree Species (Utility Compatible trees list)\" - trees marked with \"UC\" are utility-compatible. But I don't have access to that appendix directly, so I need to note this as not-verifiable.\n\nNow let me continue with my evaluation. Let me compile my findings into a structured output by evaluating each of the 47 checklist items systematically.\n\nBased on all my research, here's what I know:\n\n**KEY EVIDENCE SUMMARY:**\n1. **Overhead electric lines exist:** OHE line shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) along southern boundary\n2. **Trees proposed near OHE:** At least 3 trees within 10 feet of OHE line (Sheet 31 vision check)\n3. **Species not identified on Landscape Plan:** Trees marked as \"M\" (mitigation) or \"P\" (parking buffer) but no species labels on Sheet 31\n4. **Plant schedules exist:** Sheet 35 lists specific species - Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel\n5. **Utility-compatible marking not shown:** No indication on plans whether these species are UC-marked per ECM Appendix F\n6. **No clearance dimensions:** No dimension callouts showing horizontal clearances from conductors to trees\n7. **Building elevations:** No sheets showing overhead conductor elevations or clearances from buildings\n8. **Service drop note:** Block 17/19 mentions \"proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project\" - so distribution service drops are planned\n\n\n9. **48-hour notification:** Not found in site notes\n\nMost checklist items apply since the project involves new buildings, trees positioned near overhead lines, and various site structures. However, some items like the 15-foot radial clearance requirement would need verification of whether these are distribution lines with specific conductor types, and gas line requirements don't appear applicable to this electrical review.\n\nSubstation fencing, highway/freeway provisions, and new overhead line standards don't apply here. The overhead electrical equipment shown appears to be existing or being relocated rather than newly installed. Similarly, provisions for new power poles related to underground conversions and guy easements for transmission anchors aren't relevant to this project scope.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_read_input_tokens":69469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63269730-a4a1-4a44-9c02-2ba8ff960fa8","uuid":"5ba98cb0-9856-41b9-aae3-531dd61c3fda"}
