{"level":30,"time":1778539140081,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01StT4SMesZadGvm2FcPF2Dc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'm getting more details:\n\n1. **Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan)**:\n   - Shows overhead electric (OHE) as a dashed line with \"OHE\" text and small \"x\" marks\n   - No poles, conductors, or voltage information shown\n   - Just schematic location\n   - Trees ARE shown near the OHE line with NO clearance dimensions\n\n2. **Sheet 9 (Site Plan)**:\n   - Shows OHE running along southern and western boundaries\n   - Shows utility poles at various points\n   - Shows \"5' Electric Easement\" and \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" marked\n   - No voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission)\n   - It's assumed to be distribution (the regulatory overview says this is the default assumption for typical overhead lines unless marked otherwise)\n\nSo let me think about the checklist items now:\n\n**Applicability:**\n- **EL-2.1** (Non-UC trees within 15 ft of distribution): APPLICABLE - OHE is present and assumed distribution\n- **EL-2.2** (Non-UC trees within 50 ft of transmission): APPLICABLE conditionally - OHE is present, but only applies if it's transmission. No voltage info shown, so likely distribution. This is likely N/A.\n- **EL-2.3** (Large trees within 25 ft of distribution): APPLICABLE - OHE present\n- **EL-2.4** (Large trees within 50 ft of transmission): LIKELY N/A - assuming distribution\n- **EL-2.5** (Trees in transmission easement): LIKELY N/A - I see electric easements but no transmission easement mentioned\n- **EL-2.6** (Trees within 10 ft of poles): APPLICABLE - poles are shown\n- **EL-2.7** (Trees within 10 ft of pad-mount equipment): Need to check if pad-mounts are present\n\n\n- **EL-2.8** (Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment): Need to check if underground equipment is present\n- **EL-2.9** (Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment without root barriers): Need to check\n- **EL-2.10** (Plant legend/species identification): PASS - Species ARE identified by common and scientific names\n- **EL-2.11** (Large trees not differentiated): FAIL - The plant schedule lists installation heights (16', 10', 8') but doesn't list mature heights. For species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm, the mature height is likely 40+ feet, but this is not shown on the plant schedule.\n\nWithout notation of which trees are \"large trees,\" I can't verify compliance. **EL-2.12** and **EL-2.13** are not verifiable since no clearances are dimensioned. **EL-2.14** passes because trees and overhead equipment appear together on Sheet 31, allowing visual comparison even without dimensions. For **EL-2.15**, I need to determine if any plantings fall within prohibited zones and whether Austin Energy approvals exist. I should also verify if these species have utility-compatible designations and confirm their actual mature heights to identify which qualify as large trees.\n\nI need to examine the electrical plan more thoroughly for any clearance documentation, check pad-mount and underground equipment details, and search for Austin Energy approval correspondence.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1747,"cache_read_input_tokens":53414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1747},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8b8e89e-e0e7-4732-b385-9ef5f19fbb4a","uuid":"5e22d9fc-0d4a-49d1-a24a-f444694344c8"}
