{"level":30,"time":1778539430384,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DA1erGEosuxeYq9Ze9HmDn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for Grouping 1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Reviewed:** 47\n\n**Status Distribution:**\n- **Pass:** 3 items\n- **Fail:** 7 items  \n- **Not-Verifiable:** 22 items\n- **N/A:** 15 items\n\n### Critical Deficiencies Found\n\n**1. EL-1.14 / EL-1.27 - Retaining Wall Clearance Violation**\n- The concrete retaining wall on the south property boundary is positioned only **0.2 feet** (approximately 2.4 inches) from the overhead electric line marked on the site plan\n- **Requirement:** 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance\n- **Violation:** Absolute prohibition in UCM § 1.10.3 against installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities\n- **Action Required:** Retaining wall must be relocated away from the OHE line OR the overhead line must be relocated\n\n**2. EL-1.7 / EL-1.8 - Missing Building Elevations & Clearance Dimensions**\n- No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet site plan package\n- No section views or dimension annotations show vertical or horizontal clearances from overhead conductors to buildings or structures\n- Cannot verify compliance with surveyed conductor elevation data\n\n**3. EL-1.37 - Tree Species Not Verified**\n- Mitigation trees (\"M\" designation) are shown on landscape plan within 10 feet of overhead electric line on south boundary\n- Specific botanical species are not identified on Sheet 31 or cross-referenced to ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list\n- Cannot confirm trees meet the utility-compatible requirement\n\n**4. EL-1.46 - Missing 48-Hour Notification Requirement**\n- Sheet 3 contains a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting note, but it applies only to transmission lines\n- General 48-hour notification requirement for work near distribution-level overhead lines (UCM § 1.10.2 / Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752) is not clearly documented for applicability to all construction near the existing OHE distribution facilities\n\n### Comprehensive Assessment Provided\n\nAll findings have been documented in structured format with:\n- Specific deficiency descriptions\n- Code citations\n- Applicable areas on site\n- Sheet references\n- Agent trace documentation showing observation → reasoning → status\n\nThe structured output has been generated and is ready for applicant response and remediation planning."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12486,"cache_read_input_tokens":71327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12486},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"26e43ce3-83cf-4ed7-a640-b8c0dd12039a","uuid":"de0fe88f-33ed-4e48-be9f-e8bc94792777"}
{"level":30,"time":1778539430385,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":2361795,"duration_api_ms":204185,"num_turns":25,"result":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed the comprehensive site plan review for Grouping 1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Reviewed:** 47\n\n**Status Distribution:**\n- **Pass:** 3 items\n- **Fail:** 7 items  \n- **Not-Verifiable:** 22 items\n- **N/A:** 15 items\n\n### Critical Deficiencies Found\n\n**1. EL-1.14 / EL-1.27 - Retaining Wall Clearance Violation**\n- The concrete retaining wall on the south property boundary is positioned only **0.2 feet** (approximately 2.4 inches) from the overhead electric line marked on the site plan\n- **Requirement:** 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance\n- **Violation:** Absolute prohibition in UCM § 1.10.3 against installing customer facilities under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities\n- **Action Required:** Retaining wall must be relocated away from the OHE line OR the overhead line must be relocated\n\n**2. EL-1.7 / EL-1.8 - Missing Building Elevations & Clearance Dimensions**\n- No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet site plan package\n- No section views or dimension annotations show vertical or horizontal clearances from overhead conductors to buildings or structures\n- Cannot verify compliance with surveyed conductor elevation data\n\n**3. EL-1.37 - Tree Species Not Verified**\n- Mitigation trees (\"M\" designation) are shown on landscape plan within 10 feet of overhead electric line on south boundary\n- Specific botanical species are not identified on Sheet 31 or cross-referenced to ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list\n- Cannot confirm trees meet the utility-compatible requirement\n\n**4. EL-1.46 - Missing 48-Hour Notification Requirement**\n- Sheet 3 contains a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting note, but it applies only to transmission lines\n- General 48-hour notification requirement for work near distribution-level overhead lines (UCM § 1.10.2 / Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752) is not clearly documented for applicability to all construction near the existing OHE distribution facilities\n\n### Comprehensive Assessment Provided\n\nAll findings have been documented in structured format with:\n- Specific deficiency descriptions\n- Code citations\n- Applicable areas on site\n- Sheet references\n- Agent trace documentation showing observation → reasoning → status\n\nThe structured output has been generated and is ready for applicant response and remediation planning.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"26e43ce3-83cf-4ed7-a640-b8c0dd12039a","total_cost_usd":0.24458124999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":81,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59093,"cache_read_input_tokens":580690,"output_tokens":22513,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59093,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":81,"outputTokens":22513,"cacheReadInputTokens":580690,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59093,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24458124999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on site plan (Sheet 9) running along west and south property boundaries. Horizontal distances from OHE to buildings range from 27.9 feet to 91.3 feet (appear adequate), but no clearance dimensions labeled on plans. Cannot confirm measurement is from outside conductor vs. pole centerline, and no plan dimension annotations explicitly demonstrate 7.5-foot clearance compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 9 shows OHE markings with multiple distance measurements from conductor to building exteriors (27.9 to 91.3 feet), but no dimensional callouts on the actual plan drawing annotating or confirming clearances.","reasoning":"While measured distances suggest adequate clearance, site plan best practice requires explicit dimension annotations from outside conductor to building faces. Absence of these annotations prevents verification that the measurement methodology (from conductor, not pole) is correct or that the engineer intended compliance to be demonstrated through these distances.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8, transformers on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows underground electrical infrastructure (Sheet 21) with transformers and pull boxes. Sheet 9 shows overhead electric lines on boundaries. Without explicit radial clearance dimensions from outside conductor to customer facilities, and without utility plan clearly designating distribution vs. transmission facilities, 15-foot radial clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 site plan shows OHE lines and building locations. Sheet 21 shows electrical infrastructure with transformers and meters. No dimension annotations showing 15-foot radial clearances from outside conductor to any customer facilities.","reasoning":"Radial clearance requirement (15-foot in all directions from conductor) requires explicit documentation on utility plan showing conductor location, facility location, and measured distance. Absence of this documentation prevents verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan package (confirmed via Sheet 1 index). Without elevation sheets showing building projections (overhangs, balconies, canopies) and their relationship to overhead conductors, clearance compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 1 provides complete sheet index listing all 39 sheets; no building elevation sheets are included. Vision analysis of the sheet list shows only site plans, landscape plans, and construction details—no architectural elevation drawings.","reasoning":"Building projections and their clearances from overhead lines require elevation view drawings with surveyed conductor locations. These drawings are not included in the submittal, making verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and all associated sheets shows 39 townhome units with parking, driveways, and landscaping. No gas service or pump canopies are shown or proposed.","reasoning":"Gas pump canopies are not part of the proposed development. This item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms beneath overhead electric facilities are proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and site sections show standard driveways, sidewalks at grade, and decomposed granite walkways. No elevated structures are shown that would be proposed under or near overhead lines.","reasoning":"Elevated walkways and platforms are not part of the proposed development. This item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near ROW"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed with setbacks from Valley View Road (west property boundary). OHE lines shown on site plan along west boundary run in ROW adjacent to site. Buildings maintain adequate horizontal distance (27+ feet) from west boundary OHE line, satisfying 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis shows OHE line along west property boundary (ROW) with buildings positioned 86+ feet away from this line. South boundary also shows OHE with building-to-line distances of 27+ feet.","reasoning":"Measured distances confirm adequate clearance from buildings to overhead lines in ROW regardless of the specific clearance standard (7.5-foot or 15-foot). Requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings and structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are included in the site plan package. Without these elevation sheets, required clearances from overhead lines cannot be demonstrated as compliant.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 1 sheet index reviewed; complete 39-sheet list shows no building elevation sheets. Site plan, landscape plan, and construction details provided, but no architectural elevations showing conductor elevations with clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires surveyed elevation data on building elevation sheets. These sheets are not provided, representing a documentation failure.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings and structures throughout site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plan and section view exhibits on Sheets 9 and 21 do not show dimension lines from outer electric conductor to outermost building edges for clearance verification. OHE lines are shown symbolically but clearance dimensions are not annotated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 9 site plan shows OHE lines marked symbolically but with no dimension callouts measuring clearance from conductor to buildings. Sheet 21 electrical plan focuses on underground utilities and transformers without overhead clearance annotations.","reasoning":"Clear dimension annotations from outside conductor to building edges are necessary for compliance verification. Their absence is a documentation deficiency.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Property perimeter fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows property boundary fences marked with 'X' symbols. Fences are shown at property lines, which maintain distances greater than 7.5 feet from overhead electric lines shown on western and southern boundaries.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows fences at property boundaries. Vision analysis indicates fences positioned at property lines with OHE lines shown 27+ feet away on south boundary and 86+ feet away on west boundary.","reasoning":"Measured distances from fences to overhead conductors exceed 7.5-foot minimum requirement, satisfying clearance standard.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fence posts are shown within 10 feet of existing electric poles on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan shows boundary fences at property lines. No fence post locations are specifically marked or dimensioned relative to electric pole locations.","reasoning":"Fence posts are not shown in conflict with electric poles. This item is not applicable to the proposed work.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences are proposed adjacent to or connecting with Austin Energy substation property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan, utility plans, and easement data shows no electric substation on or immediately adjacent to the project site.","reasoning":"Substation fence isolation requirements are not triggered. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines identified on property. OHE markings on landscape plan indicate distribution facilities (lower voltage, <60kV), not transmission (≥60kV). No transmission line adjacent clearance issues apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan labels utility lines as 'OHE' (overhead electric) without transmission designation. Sheet 3 notes reference both 'Electric Transmission Notes' and 'Electric Notes', but the site-specific clearances mentioned are for distribution-level work (not transmission structures).","reasoning":"Transmission facilities operate at 69kV or higher and are physically distinct (tall towers, wide spans). Distribution facilities at typical 12.47kV or 34.5kV operate with different standards. The OHE shown is distribution, not transmission. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["South property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows property boundary fences but no explicit vehicle barrier posts are identified separate from property boundary fencing. If fencing serves as vehicle barrier beneath OHE lines, section exhibits showing 7.5-foot vertical clearance are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows boundary fences (marked with X) at property perimeter where OHE line runs. No separate section view shows vertical clearance dimensions from OHE line to fence top.","reasoning":"Whether boundary fence functions as vehicle barrier and whether vertical clearance is adequate cannot be determined without section exhibits showing conductor height and fence height with dimensions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["South property line retaining wall"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Concrete retaining wall running parallel to south property line is positioned only 0.2 feet (approximately 2.4 inches) from overhead electric line marked on site plan. This distance is far less than the required 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measurement of Sheet 9 site plan shows retaining wall running parallel to OHE line on south boundary with only 0.2-foot separation. Wall is essentially touching the conductor envelope.","reasoning":"The 0.2-foot clearance represents a critical safety violation. The 7.5-foot clearance requirement is not met. Retaining wall position must be relocated away from overhead line or line must be relocated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and utility plans shows no electric substation on or immediately adjacent to project boundaries.","reasoning":"Substation wall separation requirements are not triggered. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated platforms are proposed on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard pedestrian walkways and driveways at grade. No elevated emergency access structures are indicated.","reasoning":"Emergency access structure clearance requirements do not apply. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["South property retaining wall"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wall Plan sheets (38 and 39) provide structural reinforcement details and cross-sections but do not show dimension from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of retaining wall for clearance verification. No section view shows the spatial relationship between OHE line and wall relative to required 7.5-foot horizontal clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38 and 39 wall details focus on structural reinforcement (rebar spacing, footing dimensions, soil bearing) but do not include clearance dimensions from overhead electric line to wall face.","reasoning":"Documentation standard requires section views showing clearance dimensions from conductor to wall. This documentation is absent, representing a compliance documentation failure.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Site driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways are shown on site plan and grading plan with finished elevations. Overhead electric lines are shown on landscape plan, but vertical clearance dimensions from lowest point of OHE (including any attachments) to driveway surface are not dimensioned on section views. Truck traffic applicability (requiring 18-foot vs. 16-foot clearance) is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows driveway alignments; grading plan provides elevation data. OHE is marked on landscape plan. However, no section view shows vertical separation between driveway surface and overhead line with dimension callout.","reasoning":"Without surveyed driveway elevation and overhead line elevation with explicit clearance dimensions, and without documentation of whether truck traffic will occur, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads beneath overhead electric lines are proposed. Parking is in garage structures or surface lot on pavement, not displayed on pads under overhead lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows 10 surface parking spaces and 78 garage parking spaces in multi-story structures. No vehicle display areas or on-pad parking locations are shown beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"Vehicle parking displays on concrete pads are not part of the proposed development. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) identified on or immediately adjacent to the site. OHE markings indicate distribution facilities (<60kV), not transmission. Transmission clearance requirement (30-foot vertical minimum) does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site utility data and electric notes distinguish between 'Electric Transmission Notes' (describing transmission line safety protocols) and site-specific OHE markings. The OHE shown on plans is distribution-level infrastructure.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are not present at the site. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway grading with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures is shown. Site is small-scale residential project with local streets only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows local driveway system serving townhome complex. No highway or freeway infrastructure exists or is proposed.","reasoning":"Highway/freeway clearance from distribution underbuilt on transmission structures is not applicable. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing electric poles are not shown in conflict with proposed driveways on the site plan. Driveways are positioned in interior of site, not at boundaries where poles might exist.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows driveway layout within site boundaries. Existing utility pole locations (if any) shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) are not in direct conflict with proposed driveway alignments.","reasoning":"No pole relocation requirement triggered. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Throughout site plan where clearances dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to structures are not explicitly shown on the site plan with dimensional callouts. Where distances were measurable from plan geometry, measurement methodology (from outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be verified from plan annotations. No dimension lines originate clearly from conductor locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows OHE marking but no dimension annotations with measurement lines extending from conductor to nearby features. Without explicit callouts, measurement origin point cannot be verified.","reasoning":"Plan standard practice requires dimension lines showing measurement origin and terminus. Absence of these annotations prevents verification of proper measurement methodology per code requirement to measure from outside conductor, not pole.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Exterior lighting"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed streetlight poles (if any) shown on site plan are not located directly beneath overhead electric lines. Site lighting is shown on building-mounted fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5 compliance notes on Sheet 9.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan Block 1 notes that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5, with site lighting to be located on buildings. No pole-mounted streetlights are shown beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"Site design avoids pole-mounted streetlights under overhead lines through building-mounted lighting approach. Requirement satisfied.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Property boundary sidewalks along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed sidewalks are shown along property boundaries. Whether existing power poles are located at or near property ends along ROW where sidewalks terminate cannot be definitively determined from plans submitted, as existing pole locations from adjacent ROW properties are not detailed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and landscape plan show sidewalks at property boundaries including along Valley View Road frontage. Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) notes utility lines and poles but specific locations of adjacent ROW poles relative to sidewalk termination points are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"Pole location data for adjacent ROW is not provided in sufficient detail to verify whether sidewalks conflict with existing pole positions. Verification would require clearer existing utility infrastructure mapping.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash collection area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan Block 7 (Sheet 9) states trash containers shall not be left at curbside unattended and signage is required. However, location of trash enclosure or receptacle collection area is not precisely shown on site plan. If trash receptacles are located beneath overhead electric facilities, vertical clearance when bins are raised during service cannot be verified without section views showing conductor height and bin raised height.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 includes trash collection requirements but specific trash enclosure location is not clearly identified on the plan drawing. No section view shows trash area vertical clearance from overhead lines.","reasoning":"Trash enclosure location and overhead line proximity relationship is unclear from plans. Clearance verification would require precise location and vertical section view.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["South property retaining wall"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Concrete retaining wall on south property boundary is positioned approximately 0.2 feet from overhead distribution electric line shown on site plan. This location violates the absolute prohibition in UCM § 1.10.3 against installing customer facilities (structures) under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities, separate from clearance distance requirements. The wall must be relocated or the overhead line must be relocated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of Sheet 9 confirms retaining wall position at only 0.2 feet from OHE line running along south property boundary. The wall is directly adjacent to the conductor envelope.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 prohibits customer facilities 'under or over' Austin Energy distribution facilities absolutely, independent of clearance distances. The retaining wall is essentially at the same location as the conductor, violating this prohibition.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan does not clearly show water meter locations with dimensions to overhead electric service lines. Utility Plan shows underground water lines but meter locations relative to overhead conductors are not dimensioned. Cannot verify 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor of overhead service drops.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, meters) but water meter locations are not explicitly identified. Service drop conductor routing relative to meter locations cannot be determined from available plans.","reasoning":"Water meter clearance verification requires showing meter location and overhead service drop location with distance dimensions. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility tap plans (Sheets 19-20) connecting to proposed buildings. Overhead electric lines shown on landscape plan and site plan, but plans do not dimensionally show clearances between water line routing and overhead conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19-20 show water service connections; Sheet 31 landscape plan shows OHE markings. However, no cross-reference with dimension annotations shows clearance between these utilities.","reasoning":"Clearance verification between water lines and overhead electric requires dimensional documentation. This is not provided on plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building foundations near property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings with distances from property lines. Whether permanent foundations are within 5 feet of property line and whether electric facilities exist on adjacent properties in ROW require confirmation from utility companies. Plans show electric lines on west and south boundaries but do not confirm sufficient clearance space for utility installation on adjacent properties.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building setbacks from property lines. Exact distances from foundations to property line are not all explicitly dimensioned. Existing and proposed electric facility locations on adjacent properties in ROW are not detailed.","reasoning":"Verification requires coordination with Austin Energy to confirm space available for electric facilities on adjacent ROW. This coordination is not documented.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Site driveways and structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan shows site elevations. Overhead lines are marked on site plan and landscape plan. However, surveyed mid-span clearance data from registered surveyor is not provided. Without this data, vertical clearance from driveway surface to lowest point of overhead conductors (including attachments and sag at maximum load/temperature) cannot be verified as meeting 16-foot or 18-foot minimums.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan provides general site elevation data. OHE lines are marked on landscape plan. However, surveyor field measurements of actual conductor heights, sag, and mid-span clearances are not provided as attachments or noted on plans.","reasoning":"Code-compliant clearance verification for driveways requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance measurements accounting for conductor sag under load. These measurements are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Valley View Road crossing (if new lines)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows overhead electric lines running generally parallel to property boundaries (east-west and north-south). If new overhead electric lines cross Valley View Road, their crossing angle relative to roadway centerline cannot be verified from site plans, as no overhead line relocation or new line work is documented on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows OHE as existing facilities marked with symbols and labels. No note indicates new overhead line crossings or installations are proposed.","reasoning":"No new overhead line work appears to be proposed. Item not applicable unless project documentation exists elsewhere.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Electric infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan shows underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, meters) but does not clearly distinguish between secondary and primary overhead electric lines or show section views of line crossings. Without utility plan clearly identifying line types, crossing order cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan focuses on underground service routing. Overhead line type designations (primary vs. secondary) and crossing configuration are not shown in detail.","reasoning":"Secondary-over-primary line crossing verification requires detailed utility plan section views. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and building plan sheets show townhome residential structures without marquee signage. Signage compliance items noted on Sheet 9 refer to standard building/street address signage.","reasoning":"Marquee sign clearance requirements do not apply. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are shown on the site plan. Electrical service is proposed via underground lines shown on Sheet 21.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan shows only underground electrical routing and pad-mounted transformers. No new pole installations are proposed.","reasoning":"New power pole spacing requirement does not apply. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative outdoor lighting"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 9 notes indicate all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded, with site lighting located on buildings per Subchapter E 2.5. However, landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not clearly distinguish decorative lighting fixtures from general site lighting, nor does it show clearance dimensions if any decorative fixtures are placed beneath overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 Block 1 requires full cut-off building-mounted lighting. Sheet 31 landscape plan shows general site features but does not clearly identify decorative lighting locations with clearance dimensions from overhead lines.","reasoning":"If decorative lighting fixtures are proposed, their locations relative to overhead lines and clearance compliance would require dimension verification. This is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead electric line on south boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees labeled 'M' planted within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric line on south boundary. Vision analysis confirms multiple 'M' trees are visible within this clearance zone. However, the specific botanical species of these trees are not identified on Sheet 31 itself. Sheet 32 Tree List and Sheet 35 Landscape Calculations do not appear to clearly cross-reference the 'M' trees shown on the landscape plan with species names to verify they are on the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list. Without this verification, compliance cannot be confirmed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 shows 'M' (mitigation) tree symbols within 10 feet of OHE line on south boundary. The vision report noted the plan does not include a plant schedule identifying the exact botanical species for these trees or 'UC' utility compatible markings.","reasoning":"Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors must be from ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list (generally mature height ≤20 feet). The species identification is not provided on the landscape plan or is not cross-referenced clearly to the tree list sheets, preventing verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan shows transformer pad locations and electrical routing but meter locations for individual buildings are not clearly identified on the plan. Enlarged meter area details showing meter access clearances (30-inch wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) and potential obstructions (fences, walls, vegetation) are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows general electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes) but detailed meter locations and access clearance details are not shown in enlarged plan views with obstructions noted.","reasoning":"Meter installation accessibility requires detailed specification of location and obstructions. These details are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility symbols including poles, but the exact locations and heights of existing streetlight poles on adjacent properties in ROW are not clearly detailed. Site plan does not show clearances from proposed buildings to existing streetlight pole locations with dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 existing survey shows utility lines and pole symbols, but adjacent ROW streetlight locations are not precisely dimensioned relative to site boundary.","reasoning":"Verification of building clearances from existing adjacent streetlights would require more detailed existing utility mapping. This coordination data is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Site driveways and accessible paths"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) notes are limited regarding down guy wire locations from existing electric poles. Sheet 9 site plan shows proposed driveways and accessible paths but does not clearly document whether existing down guy anchor points and guy wire alignments conflict with these features. Without detailed existing utility infrastructure mapping showing guy wire locations, potential conflicts cannot be determined.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 survey includes utility line markings and pole locations but does not specifically call out down guy anchor positions or guy wire alignments. Sheet 9 site plan shows proposed features but does not reference down guy conflicts.","reasoning":"Down guy wire conflicts would be identified if existing guy infrastructure were clearly mapped and proposed features were dimensioned against them. This detailed coordination is not visible in the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission structures with angled guy wires are identified on the site or adjacent areas. Angled guy anchor easements are required only for transmission-level infrastructure (≥60kV), and the site has distribution-level facilities (OHE without transmission designation).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site utility data and electric transmission notes distinguish transmission from distribution. OHE marked on plans indicates distribution, not transmission infrastructure.","reasoning":"Transmission guy easement requirements do not apply. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Distribution pole down guy anchors (if present)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) notes and legend reference utility poles, but specific down guy anchor locations and down guy easement boundaries are not clearly marked on the survey or subsequent site plan. If down guys exist on existing distribution poles on or adjacent to the site, their anchor easement requirements (10-foot wide extending 5 feet past anchor ground entry) cannot be verified from available plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 4 shows utility pole symbols and legend including reference to utility poles, but down guy anchor point details are not specifically called out on the drawing.","reasoning":"Down guy anchor easement verification requires detailed mapping of existing pole configurations. This detail is not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformers"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 Preliminary Electrical Design Plan shows pad-mounted transformer locations but does not show section views with vertical dimensions from top of transformer equipment to any overhead electric lines that may be above or adjacent to transformers. Without section exhibits showing conductor elevations relative to transformer top, vertical clearance compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations in plan view but does not include vertical clearance details. Vertical clearance from overhead lines (if present above transformers) to transformer tops is not dimensioned.","reasoning":"Transformer clearance verification requires section view showing transformer height and overhead conductor position with dimensions. This documentation is absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations) are shown on the site plan. Transformers shown on Sheet 21 are pad-mounted in open areas, not in niche configurations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan shows pad-mounted transformers positioned in open areas of the site, not in covered niches or recessed installations.","reasoning":"Niche configuration clearance requirements apply only to covered/recessed transformer installations. This configuration is not proposed. Item not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas and equipment zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan (Sheet 5) shows temporary construction staging and control measures but does not explicitly dimension 10-foot radial clearances from overhead electric lines for construction equipment work zones, crane swing radius, or material storage areas. Without these dimension annotations, construction-phase compliance with OSHA 10-foot energized line clearance cannot be verified from the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 5 ESC plan shows temporary staging and erosion control but does not include dimension annotations showing 10-foot clearances from overhead lines to equipment zones or crane operating areas.","reasoning":"Construction clearance verification requires dimensional callouts on construction phasing/logistics plan. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Site cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes includes a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting requirement with Austin Energy but this note specifically applies to transmission lines (with reference to 20-foot OSHA clearance from energized transmission lines). The site plans show distribution-level overhead electric facilities (OHE). The general 48-hour notification requirement for work near high-voltage overhead DISTRIBUTION lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752 and UCM § 1.10.2 is NOT clearly stated on the cover sheet (Sheet 1) or general notes for applicability to all construction near the existing distribution lines shown on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 1 found no 48-hour notification requirement. Vision analysis of Sheet 3 found a 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting note but only in the 'Electric Transmission Notes' section, applying specifically to transmission line work (with specific contact names and 20-foot OSHA clearance reference).","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 requires owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work near high-voltage lines, applicable to both transmission and distribution. The transmission-specific note on Sheet 3 does not clearly cover the distribution-level OHE facilities shown throughout the site. A general distribution-level notification note applicable to the entire project near OHE lines is not clearly present on cover sheet or general notes.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Building service mast locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan package (confirmed via Sheet 1 sheet index). Without building elevations, service mast through-roof locations, heights, and roof clearance dimensions (3-foot minimum above roof, or 18-inch minimum if within 4 feet of roof edge for voltages ≤300V) cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 1 sheet list shows no architectural building elevation sheets. Absence of elevations prevents verification of service mast clearance details.","reasoning":"Service mast clearance compliance requires building elevation documentation. This is not provided.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"36a64b66-6707-4fb4-8d5a-9b55a5c1f496"}
