{"level":30,"time":1778539430386,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NgQLddC5NCJh3ePhgfnSHZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SV1LeJjkiy7f4p4Ztc8Sty","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimension callouts not provided. Building elevations, section views, or registered surveyor data showing that buildings maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric conductors not depicted on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) show proposed buildings and overhead electric line routing, but no building elevation sheets were found with conductor elevation data or clearance dimensions labeled from the outside conductor to building faces.","reasoning":"While overhead electric facilities are confirmed to exist on the site (OHE line shown on Landscape Plan), the requirement for surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations to buildings is a specific documentation requirement under UCM § 1.10.3. Without explicit clearance dimension callouts or registered surveyor data on building elevations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed structures and facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Customer facilities do not show clearance dimension verification. No dimension callouts showing minimum 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor of overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors to any customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, etc.) are depicted on site plan or utility plan sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric line (OHE) is shown on Sheet 31 passing through the site, but no plan sheets contain radial clearance dimension annotations from the conductor to customer facilities. The conductor type (primary vs. secondary) is not specified on the plans.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires verification of 15-foot radial clearance from primary and neutral conductors. Without explicit dimension callouts and without confirmation of the conductor type, compliance cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed building projections"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) lack required clearance verification exhibits. No building elevation sheets or section views showing dimensions from overhead conductors to building projections are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building floor elevations and heights are documented on Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan), but no building elevation details or section views showing building projection configurations relative to overhead electric lines were located in the plan set.","reasoning":"Verification of both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for building projections requires elevation and section views with dimension callouts from the outside conductor. These documents are not provided on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Gas pump canopies are not proposed on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan sheets (Sheet 9 main site plan, Sheet 31 landscape plan, and supplementary utility plans) shows no gas pump canopy features proposed.","reasoning":"EL-1.4 is only applicable when gas pump canopies are proposed. No evidence of gas pump canopies exists on the plans, making this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Stairs, elevated walkways, and elevated platforms are not clearly identified as separate features from standard building construction on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows buildings connected by sidewalks, pathways, and driveways, but no distinct elevated walkways, elevated platforms, or emergency access stairs separate from the main buildings are identified on Sheets 9 or 31.","reasoning":"EL-1.5 applies only when stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are explicitly proposed as separate site features. Standard building construction and floor-level pathways do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings adjacent to right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings adjacent to right-of-way lack documented setbacks and clearance verification from overhead electric facilities. Clearance dimension callouts from buildings to overhead lines shown in or adjacent to Valley View Road are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows buildings with setbacks from Valley View Road (western property boundary), and Sheet 3 notes indicate electric facilities in or near the right-of-way. However, no explicit clearance dimension annotations or setback dimensions from buildings to overhead lines in the ROW are shown on the plans.","reasoning":"Permanent clearance requirements from buildings to overhead electric facilities in adjacent ROW must be verified with explicit dimension callouts. Without dimension annotations or setback notes, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings and structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not included on any building elevation sheets to demonstrate required clearances are met. No registered surveyor certification of overhead conductor locations or mid-span clearance elevations provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all submitted plan sheets (Sheet 9 Site Plan, Sheet 31 Landscape Plan, electrical sheets, and structural details) reveals no building elevation pages, no conductor elevation data, and no registered surveyor certification of overhead facility locations or clearances.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires surveyed conductor elevation data to be included on building elevation sheets. The complete absence of such documentation constitutes a failure to meet this documentation requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings and building projections"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of buildings and building projections. No dimension lines or clearance annotations showing distances from outside conductor to building edges are present on any sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"All available plan sheets (Sheets 9, 31, 21, 22, etc.) were reviewed for section views or detailed plan views with dimension lines originating from overhead conductor locations. No such dimension callouts were found on any sheet.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires dimension annotations in both section and plan view from the outer conductor to the outermost building edge. Complete absence of such clearance dimensions constitutes non-compliance with documentation requirements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences shown on site plan lack dimension annotations showing clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric facilities. No horizontal clearance measurements from conductors to fence alignments are labeled on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan shows fence symbols (marked with 'X') along perimeter boundaries, and the OHE line is shown on the same sheet. However, no horizontal dimension callouts show the distance from the outside conductor to any fence.","reasoning":"Without explicit horizontal clearance dimension annotations from the conductor to the fence line, compliance with the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed fence posts near poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence post locations relative to electric poles not verified with dimension callouts. While fence locations are shown on plans, specific 10-foot clearance from pole locations to fence posts is not dimensioned.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows fence symbols and the OHE line location, but no electrical pole locations or fence post locations with specific dimensions are called out on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations showing the distance from pole centers/edges to fence post locations, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation exists adjacent to the proposed site, making this requirement inapplicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), utility plans, and facts.md indicates no Austin Energy substation facility on or immediately adjacent to the property.","reasoning":"EL-1.11 only applies when fences are proposed adjacent to existing Austin Energy substation fences. No substation exists on or immediately adjacent to this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to electric transmission lines on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The transmission easement noted on Sheet 3 (Blocks 13, 17) exists on the property, but the site plan does not show fencing proposed within or immediately adjacent to the transmission easement area.","reasoning":"EL-1.12 applies only when fencing is proposed beneath or adjacent to transmission lines. No such fencing is shown on the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed vehicle barriers"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vehicle barrier fencing or posts beneath overhead electric lines lack clearance verification exhibits. No section exhibits showing vertical and horizontal clearance dimensions from outermost conductor to any vehicle barriers are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows site perimeter with fence symbols, and the OHE line passes through the landscaping area. However, no vehicle barrier posts or bollards are distinctly identified, and no section views with clearance dimensions from conductors to such barriers are shown.","reasoning":"If vehicle barriers exist beneath overhead lines, they must have documented clearance verification. The absence of explicit section exhibits with clearance dimensions prevents verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed retaining walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls shown on landscape and wall detail sheets lack dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line. Clearance dimensions measured from outside conductor (not pole) not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38 and 39 (Wall Plan and Wall Plan Details) show retaining wall locations and cross-sections, and Sheet 31 shows the overall site with retaining walls and the OHE line routing. However, no clearance dimension callouts from the outside conductor to the retaining wall faces appear on any of these sheets.","reasoning":"Without explicit horizontal clearance dimension annotations from the outside conductor location to retaining wall surfaces, compliance with the 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation exists adjacent to the proposed site, making this requirement inapplicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and property facts shows no Austin Energy substation property adjacent to the Valley View Townhomes site.","reasoning":"EL-1.15 only applies when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. No substation exists on or adjacent to this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All emergency access structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Emergency access structures lack documented clearances from overhead electric facilities. If emergency bridges or elevated platforms are proposed, section views showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from outside conductor are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan (Sheet 9) does not distinctly identify any emergency access structures, bridges, or elevated platforms beyond standard building access and walkways.","reasoning":"While emergency access is a fire department requirement (noted on Sheet 3), no specific emergency access structures separate from main building exits and site pathways are identified as triggering the overhead clearance requirements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed retaining walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section exhibits lack dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of walls. Specific clearance dimension callouts from conductor to wall surface not shown on sections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 38 and 39 contain retaining wall section views and details, but these sections do not include dimension lines or annotations showing distances from overhead conductor locations to wall faces.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires section view clearance dimensions from the outer conductor to the wall. Complete absence of such dimension annotations constitutes non-compliance with documentation requirements.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed driveways and parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways and parking areas lack documented vertical clearance verification from lowest point of overhead electric facilities. No section views showing driveway grades and overhead line clearance heights with dimension callouts provided; mid-span clearance survey data not included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 9 (site plan), 11 (grading plan), and 31 (landscape plan) show proposed parking areas and driveways with spot elevations, and Sheet 31 shows the OHE line routing. However, no section views or cross-sections showing vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead lines to finished driveway/parking grades are provided.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.6.2 requires minimum 16-foot clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot clearance (with truck traffic) verified with dimensions and, if needed, registered surveyor mid-span data. Without these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads beneath overhead electric lines are proposed on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows covered parking (garage spaces within buildings) and surface parking areas, but these are not depicted as being directly beneath overhead electric lines based on Sheet 31 vision analysis showing OHE line along southern perimeter.","reasoning":"EL-1.19 applies only when vehicle parking or display pads are explicitly proposed beneath overhead lines. While parking exists on-site, it is not positioned directly beneath the OHE line.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Roads or driveways are not proposed or regraded beneath electric transmission lines requiring 30-foot vertical clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The transmission easement exists on the property (noted in Sheet 3 blocks), but the site plan does not show roads or driveways proposed to be constructed within the transmission easement area.","reasoning":"EL-1.20 applies only when roads or driveways are shown beneath transmission lines. The proposed driveways and parking are not located beneath transmission structures.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Highway or freeway grades with distribution underbuilt on transmission structures are not applicable to this townhome development.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows a 39-unit residential townhome development with internal site driveways and parking, not highway or freeway infrastructure.","reasoning":"EL-1.21 applies only to highway and freeway grading projects. This residential site plan does not involve highway construction.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Conflicts between proposed driveways and existing electric poles not clearly documented with dimension annotations showing 30-foot minimum relocation distances. If existing poles conflict with driveways, relocation documentation or clarification not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows driveway routing and utility pole symbols (marked differently from the OHE line), but no specific dimension callouts confirm whether existing poles are within 30 feet of any proposed driveway edges or whether relocation is required.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension annotations confirming either pole-to-driveway distances or relocation notes indicating poles moved 30+ feet from driveway edges, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All overhead electric facilities on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions shown throughout plans (where they exist at all) are not explicitly labeled as being measured from outside conductor. Standard practice requires dimension lines to originate from conductor location with annotations clarifying 'from outside conductor,' not from pole centerline or pole edges. No clearance dimensions appear to be provided at all on these plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of all plan sheets found no clearance dimension callouts at all for any site features relative to the overhead electric line. Where utility infrastructure is shown (e.g., OHE line on Sheet 31), there are no dimension annotations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 explicitly requires clearance measurements from the 'outside conductor.' The complete absence of clearance dimension annotations means this requirement cannot be met, and the deficiency of not specifying 'outside conductor' measurement basis is automatic.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed streetlights"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Streetlight pole locations not clearly documented relative to overhead electric line routing. No dimension callouts confirm whether proposed streetlights are positioned beneath overhead lines or clear of them.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (site plan) references lighting per Subchapter E 2.5, and Sheet 31 shows the site layout with the OHE line. However, specific streetlight fixture locations are not distinctly marked on the landscape plan with dimensions to the overhead line.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification and dimension callouts showing streetlight positions relative to overhead lines, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed sidewalks along right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk alignment at property corners not verified to be clear of existing power poles at ROW frontage. Specific clearance or relocation documentation for poles at property corners not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows the site plan with Valley View Road frontage (western boundary) and sidewalk routing indicated. However, no specific callouts confirm whether existing poles at the property corners are addressed through relocation, clearance, or other means.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations or notes clarifying the treatment of power poles at property corners where sidewalks meet the ROW, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash enclosure and receptacle locations not verified to maintain clearance from overhead electric facilities when trash bins are in raised position during service. Vertical clearance dimensions from overhead lines to raised trash bin heights not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows trash collection notes indicating trash containers are not permitted at curbside unattended, but specific trash enclosure or dumpster locations are not distinctly marked on the site plan, and no vertical clearance dimensions relative to overhead lines are shown.","reasoning":"Without specific location identification and vertical clearance dimension callouts accounting for raised bin heights, the clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed customer facilities and site features"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed customer facilities lack documented verification that structures are not installed under or over existing overhead distribution facilities, and items within electric easements lack dimension callouts confirming minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor. No easement exhibits with clearance annotations or relocation notes provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows the OHE line routing along the southern site boundary and through landscaping areas, and the site plan shows buildings and structures distributed across the site. However, no easement exhibit is provided showing the precise easement boundaries, and no clearance dimension callouts confirm that structures within easements (if any) maintain 7.5-foot clearances from the conductor.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 imposes an absolute prohibition on installing customer facilities under or over distribution lines and requires documented 7.5-foot clearances within easements. The absence of an easement exhibit with clearance annotations fails to demonstrate compliance with these requirements.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations not verified to maintain minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of overhead electric service drops. Clearance dimension callouts from service-drop conductors to meter locations not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19 (Utility Tap Plan), 20 (Utility Tap Public Plan and Profile), and 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design) show utility infrastructure including water service connections. However, specific water meter locations relative to overhead service-drop conductor routing and clearance dimensions are not shown with annotations.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts showing the distance from overhead service-drop conductors to water meter locations, compliance with the 7.5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing beneath or adjacent to overhead electrical distribution facilities not verified with clearance dimension callouts. No horizontal distance annotations confirm safe separation from poles and conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheets 19-20 show water utility connections, and Sheet 31 shows the overall site with OHE line routing. However, specific dimension callouts showing horizontal clearances from the water line trenching to overhead distribution poles and conductors are not provided.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations confirming safe clearance distances between water line routing and overhead distribution infrastructure, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All permanent structure foundations near property lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Permanent structure foundations within 5 feet of property line not verified to allow necessary clearance space for electric facilities in adjacent right-of-way or on adjacent property. Dimension annotations confirming adequate setback space not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows building locations with setbacks from Valley View Road (western boundary), but no specific dimension callouts confirm setbacks of foundations from the property line, nor do plans show anticipated electric facility locations in the adjacent ROW.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations from building foundations to property lines showing sufficient space for utility clearances, and without documentation of expected facility locations in adjacent properties, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed driveways and site features beneath overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing overhead facilities appear to provide marginal vertical clearances to proposed driveways and parking areas (estimated based on building elevations and spot grades), but registered surveyor mid-span clearance data and conductor elevation survey are not provided. Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances for 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 16-18 foot driveway/parking clearances not included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site benchmark elevations are documented (678.52' and 681.08' NAVD 88), and building FFE are provided (e.g., Building 1: 687.50'). The OHE line is shown on Sheet 31. However, no registered surveyor report with conducted mid-span clearance measurements or overhead conductor elevation data is provided to verify compliance.","reasoning":"When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to site features appears potentially marginal, UCM § 1.10.3 requires registered surveyor certification of mid-span clearances. The complete absence of such survey data constitutes non-compliance with this documentation requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New overhead electric lines are not proposed to cross roadways on this project; the overhead electric line shown is existing or part of relocation for on-site service.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The OHE line shown on Sheet 31 is part of existing or relocated infrastructure to serve the proposed buildings, not a new utility line being constructed across roadways.","reasoning":"EL-1.32 applies only to new overhead electric lines crossing proposed or existing roadways. The OHE line on this site is not a new roadway crossing installation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Secondary and primary overhead electric line crossing configuration not clearly identified on utility plans. No section details showing relative positioning of secondary lines above or below primary lines provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows the proposed distribution service routing, but the specific configuration of any secondary lines relative to primary lines (if both are present) is not explicitly documented in section views.","reasoning":"Without explicit section views or crossing detail drawings showing whether secondary lines are positioned above or below primary lines, the conformance with proper overhead line sequencing cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Marquee signs are not proposed on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), building elevations, and architectural details shows no marquee signs proposed for the townhome development.","reasoning":"EL-1.34 applies only when marquee signs are explicitly proposed. No marquee signs are shown on the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"New power poles for underground service conversion are not proposed on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical design (Sheet 21) shows underground service distribution to the proposed buildings. No new poles for underground conversion are identified on the utility plans.","reasoning":"EL-1.35 applies only when new poles are proposed for converting existing overhead service to underground. The proposed service is being installed new (not converting existing), making this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All decorative lighting locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Decorative lighting fixtures beneath existing overhead electric lines not verified to meet 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearance requirements. No photometric plan with clearance verification dimensions or relocation notes provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 requires that all exterior lighting be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5, and site lighting will be on buildings per plan notes. However, specific decorative lighting fixture locations relative to the OHE line and clearance dimensions are not explicitly documented on the photometric plan or landscape plan.","reasoning":"Without dimension callouts confirming clearances or notes documenting relocation of decorative lights from beneath overhead lines, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees proposed within 10 feet of overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors shown on landscape plan. Three proposed trees (marked M - mitigation tree, P - parking buffer point) are located within 10 feet of the OHE line per visual analysis. However, species are not specifically identified on the landscape plan. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but the specific trees within 10 feet of OHE line cannot be matched to species names with certainty. Utility-compatible designation per ECM Appendix F cannot be verified from submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 confirmed three proposed trees within 10 feet of the OHE line at the eastern end of the line. Sheet 35 contains plant schedules with species names but does not explicitly mark which specific trees are utility-compatible (UC-marked per ECM Appendix F) or which species are planted at the specific locations near the OHE line.","reasoning":"While tree species are listed on the plant schedule, the plans do not provide explicit mapping of species to specific locations near the OHE line, nor do they mark species as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F requirements. Without this documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed meter locations not verified to be clear of site feature obstructions such as fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, or building projections. No enlarged meter area details showing required working clearance space (30-inch-wide front, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) and absence of obstructions are provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows transformer pad and meter locations on the site, but no enlarged detail drawings or annotations confirm that meter locations have clear 30x36-inch minimum working space or 6.5-foot headroom free from obstructions.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.9.3.1 requires verified meter accessibility. Without enlarged detail drawings showing clear working space and absence of obstructions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings adjacent to streetlights"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed buildings and structures not verified to maintain required clearances from existing streetlight poles. Dimension annotations showing distances from buildings to streetlight locations not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows building locations and notes lighting requirements, but specific streetlight pole locations and dimension callouts showing clearances from buildings to streetlights are not explicitly marked.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations confirming distances from buildings to existing streetlight poles, the adequacy of clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Accessible paths and driveway alignments"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wires from existing electric poles not clearly identified on site plan or landscape plan. If conflicts exist between down guy locations and proposed accessible paths or driveways, resolution (pole relocation or conversion) not documented with notes or revised pole locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows utility pole symbols but does not distinguish between single-line poles, three-phase structures, or down guy cable anchors. Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) includes a legend showing utility poles, but specific down guy locations in conflict with proposed site features are not identified.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification of down guy locations and dimension callouts or relocation notes addressing conflicts with accessible routes, compliance cannot be verified. Note: Electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted or incompletely shown on site plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transmission guy anchors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Guy easements for angled guy anchors from transmission structures not clearly shown on plat or easement exhibit. If transmission guy anchors exist on site, dedicated easements showing 10-foot width either side of guy wire plus 50-foot extension beyond anchor not depicted with boundary annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 (General Notes) and Sheet 2 (Plat) reference transmission easements and structures, with detailed transmission requirements in Block 13. However, no specific easement diagram showing angled guy wire easement boundaries with the 10-foot-each-side plus 50-foot extension dimensions is provided.","reasoning":"Without explicit easement boundary drawings and dimension annotations for guy easements, the compliance with easement requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor points from distribution poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor points from distribution poles not clearly identified on plat or landscape plan. If down guy anchors exist within or adjacent to the project site, dedicated easement boundaries (10-foot width, 5-foot minimum extension past ground entry) not shown with dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows utility poles and landscape features, but down guy anchor locations are not distinctly identified or dimensioned. Sheet 2 (Plat) shows overall easements but does not distinguish down guy anchor easements from other utility easements.","reasoning":"Without explicit identification of down guy anchor locations and easement boundary drawings with required dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) shown on electrical plan lack documented vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines. Section view clearance annotations from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows transformer pad locations, but no section views or vertical clearance dimension callouts show the distance from overhead lines to transformer equipment tops.","reasoning":"Without section view clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to transformer tops, compliance with the 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations) are not proposed on this site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows pad-mounted transformer locations in standard above-grade configurations, not in niche (recessed/covered) service configurations.","reasoning":"EL-1.44 applies only to niche configurations with structures or canopies overhead requiring 35-foot internal clearance. Standard pad-mounted transformers do not trigger this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging and equipment operation zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms not verified to maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines during construction. Site logistics plan or construction sequencing plan with 10-foot clearance boundary annotations from overhead lines not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 5 (Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan) and the Sequence of Construction (Sheet 3 Block 10) address temporary facilities and construction staging, but no specific dimension annotations show 10-foot radial clearance zones around the overhead electric line.","reasoning":"Without dimension callouts or clearance zone markings on the construction logistics plan showing the required 10-foot construction clearance from energized overhead lines, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general project notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 notification requirement not documented in cover sheet or general notes.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of Sheet 1 (Cover), Sheet 3 (General Notes including Blocks 12-19), and all supplementary documents found no notation of the 48-hour Austin Energy notification requirement before work near high-voltage lines. Sheets 3 Block 13 and Block 17/19 address transmission line safety meetings but do not include the required 48-hour general notification note applicable to all work near overhead lines.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.2 references Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003, which requires property owner notification to Austin Energy 48 hours before work near high-voltage lines. This mandatory note is completely absent from the site plan documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service-mast through-roof installations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Service-mast through-roof installations not clearly identified on building elevations. If service masts penetrate roofs, minimum 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if mast within 4 feet of edge) for voltages ≤300V not documented with dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows the electrical service routing and transformer locations, but no building elevation sheets are provided showing where/if service masts penetrate building roofs, or what roof clearances are maintained.","reasoning":"Without building elevation views explicitly showing service-mast roof penetration locations and clearance dimensions, compliance with the 3-foot or 18-inch roof clearance requirement (for ≤300V) cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_read_input_tokens":69469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63269730-a4a1-4a44-9c02-2ba8ff960fa8","uuid":"caec87b5-4353-4881-a1c4-2f3f7ac16f65"}
