{"level":30,"time":1778539666124,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AYG2eo6UzEkt2a4meoGS3M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect. This confirms that:\n1. Large trees are NOT differentiated on the landscape plan\n2. No mature height specifications are shown on Sheet 31\n3. The key notes classification (SY, PL, P, M) is by function, not by size/height\n\nThis is exactly the deficiency described in EL-2.11.\n\nNow let me prepare my findings. Based on all my research, here are the items that are FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE:\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE ITEMS:**\n1. **EL-2.1** - Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft distribution\n2. **EL-2.3** - Large trees within 25 ft distribution (mature heights not documented)\n3. **EL-2.6** - Trees within 10 ft of poles\n4. **EL-2.8** - Trees within 5 ft underground equipment\n5. **EL-2.9** - Root barriers for trees within 20 ft underground equipment\n6. **EL-2.12** - Clearances measured from pole vs conductor (no clearances dimensioned)\n7. **EL-2.13** - Clearances measured from canopy vs trunk (no clearances dimensioned)\n8. **EL-2.15** - No Austin Energy approval for prohibited zone trees\n\n**FAIL ITEMS:**\n1. **EL-2.11** - Large trees not differentiated on plans\n\n**PASS ITEMS:**\n1. **EL-2.10** - Plant species are identified\n2. **EL-2.14** - Trees shown relative to overhead electric\n\n**N/A ITEMS:**\n1. **EL-2.2** - No transmission line\n2. **EL-2.4** - No transmission line\n3. **EL-2.5** - No transmission easement\n4. **EL-2.7** - No pad-mounted equipment\n\n\n5. **EL-2.12** - Clearances measured from pole vs conductor (applicability gate: only when dimensioned)\n6. **EL-2.13** - Clearances measured from canopy vs trunk (applicability gate: only when dimensioned)\n\nActually, I need to reconsider EL-2.12 and EL-2.13. Both have an applicability condition stating \"Only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans.\" Since no clearances are dimensioned anywhere on the landscape or site plans, these items don't apply and should be classified as N/A rather than NOT-VERIFIABLE.\n\nThis means my final list should be:\n- **NOT-VERIFIABLE**: EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.6, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.15 (6 items)\n- **N/A**: EL-2.12, EL-2.13 (2 items)\n\nLet me verify this is correct before finalizing.\n\nActually, I need to reconsider EL-2.6 more carefully. The applicability condition requires both overhead electric poles to be present or proposed, and trees to be proposed—both conditions are met since poles appear on the site plan and trees on the landscape plan. However, verifying the 10-foot lateral clearance requires cross-referencing between two separate sheets. The overhead electric line is depicted on the landscape plan with trees nearby, but I haven't confirmed whether specific pole locations are clearly marked in relation to those trees, making it difficult to measure the actual distances with confidence.\n\nSince the poles are documented on Sheet 9 and trees on Sheet 31 without explicit dimension callouts showing clearances, I can't definitively verify compliance—this warrants a NOT-VERIFIABLE status.\n\nFor EL-2.8 and EL-2.9, I should check whether any proposed trees conflict with underground electrical equipment shown on Sheet 21, such as transformers and pull boxes. heights not shown). For the NOT-VERIFIABLE items, the core issue is that the electrical and landscape plans don't provide dimensioned clearances between trees and infrastructure—utility compatibility isn't indicated, pole and tree locations are on separate sheets without cross-referencing, and distances to underground equipment aren't documented. This means I can't confirm whether the required clearances are actually met or if root barrier specifications apply. The PASS items include species identification, which is clearly documented on the landscape plan.\n\nFor the remaining standards, trees are shown relative to overhead electric lines on the same plan, which satisfies that requirement. Several standards don't apply here since there's no transmission line, pad-mounted equipment, or dimensioned clearances shown on the plans.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4174,"cache_read_input_tokens":64557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4174},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8b8e89e-e0e7-4732-b385-9ef5f19fbb4a","uuid":"882a91dd-4947-49e1-af90-b4b98f4cb9ed"}
