{"level":30,"time":1778539666125,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AYG2eo6UzEkt2a4meoGS3M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JkBVukNWrWq7HH8vgWnP8i","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric (OHE) lines are shown on both the Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) running along the property boundary. A plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists tree species (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) with common and scientific names, but contains no designation of utility-compatibility status per ECM Appendix F.","reasoning":"While the requirement for non-utility-compatible tree placement near distribution conductors is clearly applicable (distribution infrastructure is present), the plan set does not indicate which, if any, of the proposed species meet the utility-compatible (UC) designation criteria. Additionally, no clearance distances are dimensioned between trees and the overhead conductor on either the site plan or landscape plan, so the 15-foot threshold distance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along Valley View Road where OHE line is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric distribution line is present on site, and trees are proposed near it, but utility-compatibility status of tree species is not identified in the plant schedule, and clearance distances from the conductor are not dimensioned on the plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Examination of the site plans shows electric easements marked as '5' Electric Easement' and '5' Elec. & Tele. Easement' on the property. No transmission facilities (69kV, 138kV, or 345kV infrastructure) are labeled or identified.","reasoning":"The applicability condition for this item requires transmission lines (energized at 60kV or higher). The electric infrastructure shown is marked as distribution (5-foot easement widths are typical for distribution), not transmission. No transmission easement, transmission-class conductor, or high-voltage infrastructure labeling is present. This item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facility identified on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols near the overhead electric line. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists four primary tree species: Live Oak (installation height 16'), Cedar Elm (16'), Texas Mountain Laurel (8'), and Mexican Redbud (10'). Only installation/minimum heights are documented; mature height specifications are not provided anywhere on the plans.","reasoning":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are a subset of trees requiring special clearance distances from distribution conductors. However, the plant schedule provides only installation heights (the minimum size at planting), not mature heights. Species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm typically reach 40+ feet at maturity, but this cannot be verified from the submitted plans. Additionally, no clearance distances are dimensioned between trees and the OHE conductor. Therefore, it cannot be verified whether large trees exist in the restricted zone or what their clearances are.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near overhead electric distribution line where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule shows only installation heights (16', 10', 8'), not mature heights. Large trees (40+ feet) are not differentiated on plans. Clearance distances from distribution conductor are not dimensioned."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission facility is identified on the site plans.","reasoning":"This item applies only when transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are present. As determined for EL-2.2, the electrical infrastructure shown is distribution-class, not transmission. This item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facility identified on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan notes and easement documentation show '5' Electric Easement' designations, consistent with distribution infrastructure. No transmission easement boundaries are shown or referenced on the grading plan, site plan, or plat.","reasoning":"This item applies only when a transmission easement is present. The electric easements on site are 5-foot width, typical of distribution easements. No transmission easement is identified. This item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement identified on site."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows utility poles at various points along the overhead electric route, particularly near the driveway entrance on the western side and along the southern perimeter. Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols with circular canopy outlines. Both poles and trees exist on the same site, but pole locations are documented on Sheet 9 and tree locations on Sheet 31. No dimension lines or clearance callouts are shown on either sheet indicating the distance between trees and poles.","reasoning":"While both overhead electric poles and trees are present on the site, their relative proximity cannot be verified from the submitted plans. The poles are detailed on the site plan (Sheet 9) and trees on the landscape plan (Sheet 31), but no explicit clearance dimensions are provided to confirm the 10-foot minimum distance. Scaling and measuring from different sheets would be required, which is not an acceptable method for plan verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Property boundaries where overhead electric poles and landscaping occur"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric poles are shown on the site plan and trees on the landscape plan, but clearance distances between them are not dimensioned or analyzed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground transformers, pull boxes, and electrical meters. No pad-mounted electric equipment is depicted on the site plan.","reasoning":"This item applies only when pad-mounted electric equipment is present or proposed. The electrical equipment shown on Sheet 21 is underground (transformers, pull boxes, meters). No pad-mount transformers or pad-mounted equipment are indicated. This item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No pad-mounted electric equipment is proposed; all project electrical equipment is underground."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) shows underground transformers, pull boxes, and other underground electrical equipment on the site. Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed tree locations with symbol circles. The two plans do not include dimension callouts or clearance analysis showing the distance from tree planting locations to underground electrical equipment.","reasoning":"Underground electrical equipment exists on the site (transformers and pull boxes per Sheet 21), and trees are being planted (per Sheet 31), but the relative spacing and clearances are not documented with explicit dimensions. Without documented clearance distances, it cannot be verified that trees are not proposed within the 5-foot prohibition zone from underground equipment.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where underground electrical transformers and pull boxes are located relative to landscape planting zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electrical equipment is shown on Sheet 21 and trees on Sheet 31, but clearance distances between them are not dimensioned or documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Underground electrical transformers and pull boxes are depicted on Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan). Trees are shown on Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan). No root barrier details or specifications are called out on the landscape plan for trees proposed within any distance of underground equipment.","reasoning":"Root barriers are required only when trees are proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electrical equipment. However, the plans do not document clearances from trees to underground equipment (per EL-2.8), nor do they identify which trees, if any, might fall within the 20-foot zone requiring root barriers. Therefore, it cannot be verified whether root barriers are present where required.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near underground electrical equipment where trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier requirements cannot be verified without documented clearance distances from trees to underground electrical equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists all proposed tree species with both common names and botanical (scientific) names: Live Oak (Quercus Virginiana), Cedar Elm (Ulmus Crassifolia), Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora Secundiflora), and Mexican Redbud (Cercis Canadensis var. Mexicana).","reasoning":"The requirement is to identify tree species. The plant schedule provides both common and scientific names for all species, which fully satisfies the identification requirement. A plant legend showing species is present.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All landscaping areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant species are clearly identified on the plant schedule by common and scientific names."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) key notes classify trees as SY (Street Yard), PL (Parking Lot), P (Parking Buffer Point), and M (Mitigation). Plant schedule (Sheet 35) provides installation heights only (16' for Live Oak and Cedar Elm, 10' for Mexican Redbud, 8' for Texas Mountain Laurel). No mature height specifications are provided on either sheet. Landscape plan contains no notation or symbol differentiation identifying which trees are 'large trees' (40+ feet mature height).","reasoning":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height) are subject to stricter clearance requirements (25 feet from distribution conductors). The regulatory standard requires that large trees be differentiated on plans to allow clearance verification. The submitted plans document only installation heights, not mature heights. For species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm (which typically mature to 40+ feet), no mature height specification is provided. Additionally, no symbol or notation on the landscape plan differentiates large trees from smaller species. This deficiency—lack of mature height documentation and differentiation—is present.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where large trees are proposed, particularly near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape or plant schedule. Only installation heights are documented (16', 10', 8'), not mature heights. Plants do not include notation indicating which species will reach 40+ feet at maturity."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Site Plan (Sheet 9) contain no dimension lines or clearance callouts between trees and overhead electric conductors or poles.","reasoning":"This item's applicability condition is: 'Only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans.' Since no clearance distances are dimensioned anywhere on the submitted plans, the condition for this item does not exist. Therefore, the item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearances are dimensioned on the plans; applicability condition not met."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and Site Plan (Sheet 9) contain no dimension lines or clearance callouts between trees and overhead electric facilities.","reasoning":"This item's applicability condition is: 'Only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans.' Since no clearance distances are dimensioned on the submitted plans, the condition does not exist and the item does not apply.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No tree clearances are dimensioned on the plans; applicability condition not met."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) displays tree symbols (circular outlines representing canopy) and includes the overhead electric line labeled 'OHE' with associated dashed linetype running along the southern property boundary. Trees are shown positioned on the same drawing relative to the OHE line.","reasoning":"The requirement is that trees and overhead electric facilities be shown in relation to each other on the landscape plan to allow clearance verification. While no dimensions are provided, the trees and OHE line are both depicted on Sheet 31 on the same drawing at the same scale, allowing visual comparison of their relative positions. This satisfies the graphic requirement to show trees in relation to overhead electric.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing full site layout"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees and overhead electric facilities are both shown together on the landscape plan