omment":"Retaining walls are shown on the site plan (Sheet 11 Grading Plan and Sheet 38 Wall Plan), but no transformer pads are positioned adjacent to these walls. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are depicted on grading and wall detail sheets, but transformer pads shown on Sheet 21 are not located within proximity to these walls based on site layout.","reasoning":"The applicability gate requires that retaining walls be present adjacent to transformer pads for this requirement to apply. Since no transformer pads are adjacent to retaining walls, the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads if fences are adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows potential fencing on property boundaries, but access door orientations for transformer pads are not indicated on Sheet 21, making it impossible to determine which side is the operator side (5 feet) versus non-operator side (3 feet). Without access door orientation, the requirement cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 confirmed that transformer pad symbols are simple squares with no markings indicating access door location or orientation.","reasoning":"The 5-foot vs. 3-foot clearance requirement depends on identifying which side of the pad faces operators/controls. Since this orientation is not indicated, clearance verification is impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Any transformer pad with clearance less than 5 feet"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While one transformer pad (Bldg 7) clearly violates the 5-foot minimum, the architectural specifications showing fire ratings are not provided in the site plan set. If reduced clearances were intended, required documentation (AE Design approval, fire rating confirmation, window/door clearances, confinement verification) is not included.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads but contains no references to architectural specifications or fire rating documentation. No cross-references to detail sheets showing fire-rated construction are present.","reasoning":"Even if reduced clearances were allowed by exception, the four prerequisites (AE Design approval, fire rating documentation, window/door distance verification, non-confined space confirmation) cannot be verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or overhangs are shown directly above or adjacent to the transformer pad locations on Sheet 21. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis and review of Sheet 21 site plan shows transformer pads are located in open areas adjacent to or between buildings, with no overhead structures directly above or cantilevered overhangs shown in their immediate vicinity.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (balconies or overhangs present above/adjacent to transformer) is not met based on the plan geometry shown.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads adjacent to buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment, and transformer equipment specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not provided on Sheet 21. Additionally, building elevations and window/door locations relative to transformer pads are not shown or dimensioned. Compliance cannot be verified without equipment specifications and elevation details.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 labels transformer pads but includes no equipment specifications or callouts to elevation drawings showing window/door locations or vertical relationships.","reasoning":"Two prerequisites for verification are missing: (1) confirmation that equipment is oil-filled, and (2) building elevation drawings showing window/door positions relative to pads. Without both, the requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All five transformer pads measured 2.7 feet or greater from the nearest sidewalk, meeting the 2-foot minimum requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement tool measured distance from each of 5 transformer pads to nearest sidewalk: Bldg 1 (21.4 ft), Bldg 2 (2.7 ft), Bldg 8 (21.4 ft), Bldg 5 (10.7 ft), Bldg 7 (20.3 ft). All exceed 2-foot minimum.","reasoning":"All measured clearances are at or above the 2-foot minimum standard. The most restrictive measurement (Bldg 2 pad at 2.7 feet) still exceeds the threshold.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown adjacent to transformer pads on Sheet 21 or on the fire protection plan (Sheet 10). This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of electrical plan (Sheet 21) and fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows no stairwell structures adjacent to any transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (stairwell present adjacent to transformer) is not met, making the requirement non-applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or external stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on Sheet 21 or on building elevation/floor plan drawings. Additionally, equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 found no fire escapes or exit stairs depicted. Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows fire zones and hydrants but no fire escape structures.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when fire escapes are present and equipment is oil-filled. Neither condition is demonstrated on the plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Access door orientations are not indicated on Sheet 21 transformer pad symbols. No dashed lines, arrows, or labels show the hot-stick use area or access door location. Without this orientation, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified for any transformer pad.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed transformer pads are shown as simple squares or squares with crosshatch, with no distinguishing marks indicating door location or orientation toward any compass direction.","reasoning":"The hot-stick clearance requirement is directional—it applies specifically to the access door side. Without knowing which side is the door, the clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Any transformer in confined space or niche configuration"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations are indicated as being in niches, vaults, or enclosed areas on Sheet 21. However, access door orientations are not shown, and no cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearances in enclosed or notched-out building configurations are provided. If any transformer faces a confined space (3+ sides), the 15-foot clearance requirement and supporting cross-section documentation cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows all transformer pads in open areas between/adjacent to buildings with no notation of niche installation. No cross-sections depicting vertical clearances are referenced.","reasoning":"While the plan does not indicate niche installations, the absence of access door orientation and cross-section documentation means that if any pad does face confined space, verification would be impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["If fire hydrants are adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan) shows 1 private fire hydrant on the site. Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) shows transformer pads. However, a coordinated measurement between hydrant and transformer locations cannot be performed without both sheets overlaid or cross-referenced. Proximity cannot be conclusively determined.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire hydrant location is shown on Sheet 10, transformer pads on Sheet 21. These sheets are not directly overlaid in the submitted materials, preventing direct distance measurement.","reasoning":"Without overlaid plan sheets or explicit callouts noting proximity, the 5-foot clearance between transformer and hydrant cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["If trees are within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees labeled categorically (SY, M, FL, P) but not with species names. Tree species cannot be confirmed as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F without explicit species identification on the landscape plan or reference to a detailed plant schedule listing species and ECM utility-compatible status.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 found trees labeled only with categorical codes (SY, M, FL, P) denoting location type and mitigation status, not species names. A plant schedule with species names was not located on the provided sheet.","reasoning":"To verify utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F, the species name must be identified. The landscape plan does not provide species names directly or reference a plant schedule; therefore, verification is impossible.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["If shrubs or low vegetation are adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Access door orientations for transformer pads are not indicated on Sheet 21, so it is impossible to identify which side is the access door side (requiring 10-foot clearance) versus other sides (requiring 5-foot clearance). Additionally, specific shrub/vegetation locations relative to transformer pads cannot be precisely determined from the landscape plan without overlaid coordinate reference.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows generic vegetation symbols and categories, and Sheet 21 transformer pads lack orientation markings. Direct spatial relationship between specific shrubs and specific pad sides cannot be established.","reasoning":"The clearance requirement is directional (10 feet access side, 5 feet other sides), and without access door orientation, the directional requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["If trees are within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees but does not provide root barrier details or reference sheets containing root barrier specifications. No detail callouts or sheet references for root barrier construction are visible on the landscape plan. Root barrier presence and specifications cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) found tree symbols and categories but no detail references (e.g., 'See Sheet 37 Detail RB-1') or notes specifying root barrier installation for trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment.","reasoning":"The plan does not show or reference root barrier details. Without explicit specifications or callouts, compliance with the 4-foot depth and 5-foot setback requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown on Sheet 21 adjacent to transformer pads. This requirement