licability condition (overhead distribution lines present) is not met based on submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on any plan sheets. The 15-foot radius clearance requirement applies only when overhead conductors are present, which is not the case on this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive review of electrical plan (Sheet 21) and all utility notation shows only underground electric service. No overhead distribution infrastructure is depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead primary/neutral conductors present) is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 shows all transformer pads in open areas between or adjacent to buildings. No transformer locations are indicated as being within niches, vaults, or enclosed building footprints. No cross-section drawings are needed because niche service is not proposed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 shows all 5 transformer pads positioned externally relative to building footprints, not within notched-out or enclosed areas of building structures.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (niche service installation) is not met based on the plan configuration shown.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service is proposed on this project. All transformer pads are located external to buildings (not within building footprints). Fire wall ratings and ventilation specifications for niche service are not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 configuration shows all transformers positioned outside building structures, not within enclosed spaces. No niche installation is indicated.","reasoning":"Niche service applicability condition is not met; therefore, fire wall rating and ventilation requirements for niches do not apply.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are present above transformer pad locations. All transformers are located in open areas. Cross-section drawings are not required because no vertical clearance verification is needed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pads in open areas of the site plan with no overhead structures shown above them. Building roof lines are not depicted directly above any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead structures or enclosed areas present) is not met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads if oil-filled equipment is used"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Equipment specifications (oil-filled vs. dry-type) are not provided on Sheet 21. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows surface contours and drainage flow, but no specific callouts verify that drainage slopes away from transformer pad locations. Drainage slope direction cannot be verified without equipment type confirmation and explicit grading annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 contains no equipment specifications. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows overall site topography and contours but does not include spot elevations or slope arrows specifically around transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Verification requires two elements: (1) confirmation of oil-filled equipment, and (2) specific grading callouts showing flow direction away from pads. Neither is provided.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads shown on Sheet 21 are located within the private property boundary depicted on both the electrical plan and the plat sheet (Sheet 2). No transformer pads are positioned in public right-of-way or straddling property lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Visual analysis of Sheet 21 shows all 5 transformer pad locations positioned well within the interior property boundaries, far from the property line edges. Plat sheet (Sheet 2) confirms the private lot boundary.","reasoning":"All transformer locations are clearly within private property and not adjacent to or crossing the property line boundary.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads if located in easement areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Multiple easements are shown on the site plan (drainage easements, wastewater easements, public utility easements, electrical easements). Sheet 21 does not provide explicit callouts indicating whether transformer pads are or are not located within any of these easement areas. Without specific dimension callouts or easement boundary overlays, it cannot be verified that transformers avoid prohibited easements or that AE Design written approval (if required) has been obtained.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheets 9, 11) shows easement boundaries as dashed lines; Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations. No cross-reference callouts link transformer locations to specific easement areas, making spatial relationship unclear.","reasoning":"Verification requires determining whether each transformer is within or outside each easement type. Without explicit callouts or overlaid boundaries with dimension verification, this cannot be conclusively determined.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21, but no easement boundaries or easement dimension callouts are provided on that sheet. The existence and dimensions of transformer easements around the pads cannot be verified. Austin Energy Design accessibility requirements for easement width are not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad symbols but includes no dashed easement boundary lines, dimension callouts for easement width, or notes specifying easement size or AE Design approval of easement extent.","reasoning":"Without explicit easement boundaries and dimensions shown on the electrical plan, the existence and adequacy of transformer easements cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing from all transformer pads to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 