{"level":30,"time":1778540732801,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","retry":1,"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018t61JkWkWVRqpUap1KFQ1x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, the second vision check says there are 5 transformer pads, not 4! This is important. The first vision check found 4 pads, but now the second one is saying there are 5 pads total. And importantly, it says one of them (near Bldg. 8/Unit 703) appears to be straddling the property boundary and extending into a sidewalk easement and possibly the ROW.\n\nActually, reading more carefully: the vision check says the pad \"west of Bldg. 8\" is \"drawn directly over the vertical line that forms the western boundary\" and \"extending outward into the easement area\" near Valley View Road.\n\nThis is a clear FAIL for EL-13.33 - at least one transformer pad is not entirely on private property; it's straddling/extending into the property boundary area.\n\nFor EL-13.13 (trees), the measurements show:\n- Tree north of southwest transformer pad: 12.1 feet (outside the 10-foot requirement - PASS)\n- Tree south of southwest transformer pad: 21.9 feet (outside the 10-foot requirement - PASS)\n\nBut this is only for one pad. I need to check if there are other trees near other pads, and I need to verify the species are utility-compatible.\n\nLet me continue checking other items, particularly:\n- Drainage/grading from oil-filled transformers\n- Overhead lines clearances\n- Underground utility clearances\n- Fire hydrants\n- Sidewalk clearances\n- Fences\n- Retaining walls","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3178,"cache_read_input_tokens":66947,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3178},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier