{"level":30,"time":1778542382207,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011cegPYpSG9xkMB23uVrt4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The vision check for EL-2.8 provided detailed measurements. Key findings:\n\n1. Underground Electric Line west of Bldg 1: Tree is 5.3 feet away - JUST OVER the 5-foot threshold (barely compliant by 0.3 feet)\n2. Electrical Transformer Pad west of Bldg 8: Tree is 6.9 feet away - compliant\n3. Electrical Transformer Pad west of Bldg 2: Tree is 21.6 feet away - this tree is within 20 feet so would need root barriers\n\nThe measurement showing 5.3 feet is interesting - it's just barely over 5 feet. But more importantly, the vision check shows that measurements ARE being made on Sheet 21, which is the electrical design plan, not the landscape plan.\n\nHowever, I need to verify whether these measurements are documented on the landscape plan or if this is just what the vision specialist measured visually. Let me check if the landscape plan shows these clearances dimensioned.\n\nAlso, for EL-2.9, I need to check if root barriers are shown in the details on Sheet 37.\n\nLet me look at what the vision check found for EL-2.8:\n- There is at least one tree within 5.3 feet of underground electric equipment (just barely over the 5-foot minimum)\n- There is a tree within 21.6 feet of a transformer pad (west of Bldg 2)\n\nFor EL-2.9, I need to know if root barriers are specified for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment.\n\nLet me also check the landscape details sheet.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2085,"cache_read_input_tokens":58106,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2085},"output_tokens":2,"ser