{"level":30,"time":1778542460584,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013fw7L1Uu4k1njK3PW4hVy7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016LoR2MTiZwkWkkrUNYsFeN","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 2","Transformer pad east of Building 7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two transformer pads are located at 0 feet clearance from building exterior walls (west of Building 2 and east of Building 7), falling short of the required 5-foot minimum clearance from buildings, structures, and building foundations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measured clearances from transformer pads to nearest building walls. Two transformer pads (west of Bldg 2 and east of Bldg 7) measured at 0 feet distance from the building exterior walls on Sheet 21.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings. A 0-foot clearance indicates the transformer pad is touching or abutting the building wall, which constitutes non-compliance with the stated minimum.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad located between Buildings 3 and 5"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located between Buildings 3 and 5 has only 3.2 feet clearance to the nearest building (Building 3), which falls short of the required minimum 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance to adjacent buildings or structures on the access door side.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measured the clearance from the transformer pad between Bldgs 3 and 5 to Building 3's east exterior wall at 3.2 feet on Sheet 21.","reasoning":"The hot-stick use area (access door side) requires minimum 10-foot clearance to adjacent buildings or open areas. A 3.2-foot clearance is significantly less than required, indicating non-compliance unless this is the non-access side direction.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire lane on site","Transformer pad west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located west of Building 8 is only 3.5 feet from the fire lane boundary, which fails to meet the required minimum 15-foot clearance from fire lanes.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measured the distance from the transformer pad west of Building 8 to the nearest fire lane boundary as 3.5 feet on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan).","reasoning":"The code requirement specifies minimum 15-foot clearance from fire lanes. A 3.5-foot clearance is approximately 4.3 times less than required, indicating clear non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 (easement-specific regulations)"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad east of Building 4/5 area","Transformer pad east of Building 7 area","25' Drainage Easement","15' Easement","5' Electric Easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two transformer pads are located within prohibited easements without documented Austin Energy Design written approval. One pad (east of Building 4/5) is located within the 25' Drainage Easement (Document 2011021707). Another pad (east of Building 7) is located within overlapping 15' Easement and 5' Electric Easement boundaries. Transformer equipment cannot be placed in drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements under overhead lines without written AE Design approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check identified dashed easement boundary lines on Sheet 21 labeled as '25' Drainage Easement Doc. 2011021707' and '15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76' and '5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14'. Transformer pad symbols were observed within these dashed boundaries.","reasoning":"The regulatory framework prohibits transformer placement in drainage, water, sewer, or electrical easements. The visual evidence shows transformer pads drawn within easement boundaries on the plan. No documentation of AE Design written approval was found in the submitted materials.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site","All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No separate transformer easements are shown on the site plan or plat. The plat (Sheet 2) shows only general utility easements (15' PUE, 26' Drainage Easement, 10' Water & Wastewater Easement) but contains no designated transformer easements with specified widths for Austin Energy accessibility requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of plat sheet found several recorded easements labeled (15' PUE, 26' Drainage Easement, 10' Water & Wastewater Easement) but found no easements specifically labeled as 'Transformer Easement' or similar designation.","reasoning":"Code requires transformer easements to be shown around pads with width determined by AE Design for accessibility. The absence of any labeled transformer easements on the plat indicates this required element is missing from the submission.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing on south side of property"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical service line routing (shown in blue on Sheet 21) on the south side of the property measures 0 feet from the south property boundary line, indicating the line runs along or potentially crosses the property line. It cannot be verified from the available plan whether the electrical routing from transformers to meters remains 100% on private property or if portions extend into the public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measured the distance from the blue underground electrical line on the south side of the site to the south property boundary line and returned 0 feet, meaning the line is at the boundary.","reasoning":"A 0-foot measurement indicates the electrical line is at the property boundary. The code requires 100% private property routing. A line at the boundary is ambiguous—it could be inside, outside, or straddling the property line—which creates an unresolvable verification gap from the available plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions (length x width) are not labeled on the site plan. No references are provided to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets or specifications for the proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase). The plan cannot be verified against AE Design standard pad dimensions for the specified electrical service configuration.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 21 shows transformer pads labeled with text 'Electrical Transformer Pad' but found no dimensional callouts (e.g., '5'x5'', '10'x10'') and no references to detail sheets such as 'AE Design Detail' or 'Per Austin Energy Standard Pad' in the plan notes.","reasoning":"The code requires pad dimensions to match AE Design-approved specifications for the service type. Without dimensions shown or references to AE Design details, the compliance of the pad size cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 1","Parking area curb and driveway circulation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located west of Building 1 is positioned less than 4 feet from a concrete curb and gutter forming the edge of a drive aisle/parking circulation area. No 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards are shown or labeled around this transformer pad to provide vehicle impact protection, nor are bollards shown around any of the other transformer pads on the site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check identified a transformer pad labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' immediately adjacent to a line labeled 'Concrete Curb & Gutter' forming a curved driveway on Sheet 21, with the measured distance less than 4 feet. A separate visual analysis confirmed no bollards are labeled or shown around any of the four transformer pad locations on the plan.","reasoning":"When transformer equipment is within 4 feet of parking or vehicle routes, bollards are required per AE Design equipment pad details. The absence of bollard symbols, callouts, or references indicates this protective element is missing from the design.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations shown on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not labeled or identified on the grading plan (Sheet 11). Without visible transformer pad locations on the grading plan, surface drainage slopes around transformer locations cannot be assessed. Additionally, the transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan, making it impossible to verify whether drainage must flow away from buildings or if special drainage considerations apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 11 (Grading Plan) examined the plan for labeled transformer pads and found none identified on that sheet, though electrical easement labels were present. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not include specifications indicating whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment, which must have drainage directed away from buildings. Without transformer pad identification on the grading plan and without equipment type specification, the grading compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads","Retaining walls on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located at minimum distances of 126.6 feet or greater from the nearest retaining walls on the site, exceeding the required 5-foot minimum clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks measured distances from each transformer pad to the nearest existing stone retaining wall on the east side of the site, with results ranging from 126.6 to 392.4 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances (126+ feet) are substantially greater than the required 5-foot minimum, indicating full compliance with the retaining wall clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fences or gates are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 21 found no fence or gate symbols adjacent to any of the labeled transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The requirement is conditional and only applies when fences or gates are present adjacent to transformer pads. The absence of such features means this item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer pads are shown with clearances less than 5 feet to brick/masonry buildings (except for the non-compliant 0-foot clearances already flagged under EL-13.1). Therefore, the reduced clearance exception documentation requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of clearance measurements found that transformer pads either have greater than 5 feet clearance (passing requirement) or zero feet (failing requirement). No cases of reduced clearances (3-5 feet) that would require exception documentation were found.","reasoning":"The reduced clearance exception is only applicable when a project seeks to implement the 3-foot alternative. Since no 3-5 foot clearances are shown, this item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No balconies or overhangs are shown above transformer pad locations on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of building elevations and site plan layout shows no balconies, overhangs, or covering structures positioned above any transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when balconies or overhangs are present above or immediately adjacent to transformers. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No windows, doors, or ventilating ducts on adjacent buildings are shown within the proximity ranges that would trigger the 12-foot oil-filled equipment clearance requirement. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of building locations and site plan layout found no windows, doors, or ducts positioned on adjacent buildings within the critical clearance zones (less than 12 feet with inadequate lateral separation).","reasoning":"The requirement is conditional on the presence of windows, doors, or ducts in proximity. Their absence in the critical zones makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No sidewalks are shown adjacent to or immediately abutting transformer pad locations on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows sidewalks and walkways but none positioned immediately adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The 2-foot clearance requirement applies only when sidewalks are adjacent to transformers. The absence of such adjacency makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells serving as fire exits are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and building floor plan references found no stairwells labeled as fire exits or emergency exits positioned adjacent to transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when stairwells are present adjacent to transformers. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the site plan or building elevations. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of fire protection plan (Sheet 10) and site plan found no fire escape symbols or labels adjacent to any buildings or transformer locations.","reasoning":"The 20-foot clearance requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment with fire escapes present. The absence of fire escapes makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad located between Buildings 3 and 5"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad located between Buildings 3 and 5 has only 3.2 feet clearance to the nearest building (Building 3), which falls short of the required minimum 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance to adjacent buildings or structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check measured the clearance from the transformer pad between Bldgs 3 and 5 to Building 3's nearest exterior wall at 3.2 feet on Sheet 21.","reasoning":"The hot-stick use area requires minimum 10-foot clearance on the access door side. A 3.2-foot clearance is significantly less than required, indicating non-compliance with the stated minimum clearance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not located in confined spaces, niches, vaults, or notched-out building configurations. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and building configurations shows all transformer pads located in open areas of the site, not within or adjacent to enclosed structures or notched building areas.","reasoning":"The 15-foot clearance requirement applies only when transformers face confined spaces (niches, vaults, enclosed areas on 3+ sides). The absence of such configurations makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire hydrant location","Transformer pad west of Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The single proposed fire hydrant shown on the fire protection plan is located 28.9 feet from the nearest transformer pad (west of Building 8), exceeding the required 5-foot minimum clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 10 identified one fire hydrant symbol at the southwest driveway entrance and measured its distance to the transformer pad west of Building 8 as 28.9 feet.","reasoning":"The measured distance (28.9 feet) significantly exceeds the required 5-foot minimum, indicating full compliance with the fire hydrant clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near transformer pads on landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees identified on the landscape plan within proximity to transformer pads are either at or beyond the 10-foot lateral distance requirement (measured at 11.2 and 20 feet from the nearest transformer pad). The requirement for utility-compatible species identification appears to not be triggered by the current design.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 31 identified two trees (labeled 'SYM' and 'M') near the southwest transformer pad location, with measured distances of 11.2 feet and 20 feet respectively.","reasoning":"The requirement applies to trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment. With trees at or beyond 10 feet, the utility-compatibility verification requirement is not triggered, and the requirement passes by inapplicability.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No shrubs, low-lying vegetation, or landscaping is shown on the landscape plan adjacent to or within the clearance zones of transformer pad locations. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of landscape plan (Sheet 31) found minimal plantings adjacent to transformer pad locations, with primary landscaping concentrated in parking lot islands and common open space areas away from the pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when shrubs or vegetation are proposed adjacent to transformers. The absence of such plantings in proximity to pads makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No trees are shown on the landscape plan within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment (transformer pads). This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of landscape plan (Sheet 31) and vision checks of tree locations relative to transformer pads found no trees within the 20-foot critical distance that would trigger root barrier requirements.","reasoning":"The root barrier requirement applies only to trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. The absence of trees in this proximity makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) found no dumpster, trash bin, or enclosure symbols adjacent to transformer pad locations or elsewhere on the site.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when dumpsters are present. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bike racks are shown on the site plan in parking lot areas (per Sheet 9 bicycle parking callouts) but are not positioned adjacent to transformer pad locations. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) identified 41 bicycle parking spaces (39 long-term, 2 short-term) but found no bike rack symbols adjacent to any transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"The 5-foot clearance requirement applies only when bike racks are adjacent to transformers. The absence of such adjacency makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No light poles are shown on the site plan adjacent to transformer pad locations. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of landscape plan (Sheet 31) and site plan (Sheet 9) found no light pole symbols positioned adjacent to any transformer pads.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when light poles are adjacent to transformers. Their absence in proximity to pads makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Only one set of transformer pads is shown on the electrical plan, or multiple pads do not overlap. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 21 identified multiple individual transformer pad locations, but they are distributed across the site and do not have another transformer pad as a neighboring feature requiring 5-foot separation.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when multiple transformer pads are located in proximity requiring separation from one another. With each pad standing alone in its location, this requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads","Water service lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from water lines. Measured distances range from 11.7 feet to 60.9 feet from the nearest water utility.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks measured clearances from each transformer pad to the nearest water line (marked -W- on Sheet 21), with results of 46.2 feet, 11.7 feet, 60.9 feet, 32.7 feet, and 44 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances meet or exceed the required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water lines, indicating full compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads","Wastewater service lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from wastewater lines. Measured distances range from 12.2 feet to 82.5 feet from the nearest wastewater utility.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks measured clearances from each transformer pad to the nearest wastewater line (marked -WW- on Sheet 21), with results of 12.2 feet, 82.5 feet, 67.7 feet, 19.4 feet, and 29.9 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances meet or exceed the required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from wastewater lines, indicating full compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads","Storm drain lines and inlets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads maintain minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from storm drain lines and inlets. Measured distances range from 27.9 feet to 73.6 feet from the nearest storm drain structure.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks measured clearances from each transformer pad to the nearest storm drain line or inlet (marked -SD- on Sheet 21), with results of 63.1 feet, 52.6 feet, 27.9 feet, 37.5 feet, and 73.6 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances substantially exceed the required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from storm drain lines, indicating full compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service is shown on the utility tap plan (Sheet 19) or any other utility plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 19 (Utility Tap Plan) listing utility specifications shows only water, wastewater, storm drain, and electrical utilities. No gas service or pipeline infrastructure is identified.","reasoning":"The gas line clearance requirement applies only when gas service is present on the project. The absence of gas service makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads","Underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4