":"No overhead distribution lines or conductors are shown on the site plan or electrical plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows only underground electrical service, with no overhead distribution lines, poles, or conductors depicted.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement applies only when overhead distribution lines are present. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are shown on the site plan. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) indicates all electrical service is underground, with no overhead distribution conductors or poles shown.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance requirement applies only when overhead distribution primary or neutral conductors are present. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not located in niches, enclosed areas, or notched-out building configurations. All transformers are installed in open areas of the site. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 21) and building floor plans shows all transformer pads located in open areas outside building footprints, not in any enclosed or notched-out locations.","reasoning":"The 35-foot vertical clearance requirement applies only to niche installations where transformers are accessible from outside but located within building footprints. The absence of such configuration makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are proposed. Transformer pads are located in standard open areas outside building envelopes. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical plan (Sheet 21) and architectural plans shows all proposed transformers as standard pad-mounted units in open areas, not as niche installations within building footprints.","reasoning":"The fire wall rating and ventilation requirements apply only to niche service installations. The absence of niche service makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are shown above transformer pad locations that would require cross-section drawings demonstrating vertical clearances. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 21) and building elevations shows no overhead structures, canopies, parking garages, or enclosed areas above any transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances are required only when overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas exist above transformers. Their absence makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located 100% on private property, with minimum clearances of 6.1 feet or greater from the property boundary line. No transformer pads straddle property lines or extend into the public right-of-way.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks measured clearances from each transformer pad to the nearest property boundary, with results of 33.7 feet, 11.1 feet, 6.1 feet, 92.4 feet, and 48.7 feet. All measurements show positive distances inward from the property line.","reasoning":"All measured distances are positive values from the property boundary, indicating all transformer pads are located fully on private property, meeting the requirement that equipment be 100% on private property.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead distribution facilities are shown on the site plan. Therefore, no customer buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks, or other structures are located under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. This requirement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 21) and electrical plan shows all electrical service is underground, with no overhead distribution lines, poles, or other overhead facilities depicted.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only when overhead distribution facilities are present on the site. The absence of such facilities makes this requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_detail