howing a tree with a chain link fence around it. The fence is labeled 'TREE PROTECTION FENCE' and 'CRITICAL ROOT ZONE'. The area inside the fence is labeled 'WOOD CHIP MULCH AREA 100mm - 150mm (4\"-6\") DEPTH'. Dimensions are given as '6m FOR 500mm DIA. TREE (20'-0\" FOR 20\" DIA. TREE)' and 'DRIPLINE'. The limits of the critical root zone are labeled 'LIMITS OF CRITICAL ROOT ZONE RADIUS = 12mm PER mm (1ft PER in) OF TRUNK DIAMETER'. A note reads '*AS NEEDED TO PROVIDE MINIMUM NECESSARY WORK SPACE. IF LESS THAN 1.5m (5'), THEN ADD BOARDS STRAPPED TO TRUNK.' A smaller illustration to the left shows a tree with a fence around it, labeled '24m (8')' and '1.5m (5')*'. A note below reads 'VARIES'. A line points to a building to the right, labeled 'BUILDING'.]\n    29→\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8aec104c-0835-4d66-891b-4f34e6fe876f","uuid":"33415579-7785-435f-8c7e-2fb802e8cae0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-37/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 37 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — Detail drawing and notes for planting shrubs.\n\nSHRUB PLANTING, REF. PLAN\n\n[Drawing of two shrubs planted in the ground, showing the root ball, amended soil mix, and undisturbed earth. The planting hole is labeled '15\"'. The soil surface is covered with a layer labeled '3\" DEPTH ORGANIC WOOD MULCH CONTINUOUS AMENDED SOIL MIX, NO PLANTING WILL BE ALLOWED IN POCKETS OF ISOLATED NEW SOIL.' The soil below the shrubs is labeled 'UNDISTURBED EARTH'.]\n\nNOTE:\nCONTRACTOR TO REMOVE DIRT, DEBRIS, & FILL AS NECESSARY TO ALLOW FOR AMENDED SOIL MIX. LANDSCAPE CONTRACTOR SHALL COORDINATE WITH THE GENERAL CONTRACTOR AND EARTHWORK CONTRACTOR TO ENSURE THAT THE PROPER GRADES AND MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED. IF MATERIAL IS REQUIRED TO BE BROUGHT IN AS FILL OR REMOVED FROM SITE AS CUT THE CONTRACTORS SHALL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR COORDINATING THAT WORK.\n\n3 SHRUB PLANTING\nScale: 1/2\" = 1'-0\"\n\n## Block 2: diagram — Standard detail for tree protection fence as required by the City of Austin. Shows a top view of a tree and building with the critical root zone, dripline, and limits of critical root zone. Also includes a detail view of a tree with dimensions for tree protection fence.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nWATERSHED PROTECTION DEPARTMENT\nTREE PROTECTION FENCE\nMODIFIED TYPE A - CHAIN LINK\nRECORD COPY SIGNED BY J. PATRICK MURPHY\n11/15/99\nADOPTED\nTHE ARCHITECT/ENGINEER ASSUMES RESPONSIBILITY FOR APPROPRIATE USE OF THIS STANDARD.\nSTANDARD NO.\n610S-4\n\n[Illustration showing a tree with a chain link fence around it. The fence is labeled 'TREE PROTECTION FENCE' and 'CRITICAL ROOT ZONE'. The area inside the fence is labeled 'WOOD CHIP MULCH AREA 100mm - 150mm (4\"-6\") DEPTH'. Dimensions are given as '6m FOR 500mm DIA. TREE (20'-0\" FOR 20\" DIA. TREE)' and 'DRIPLINE'. The limits of the critical root zone are labeled 'LIMITS OF CRITICAL ROOT ZONE RADIUS = 12mm PER mm (1ft PER in) OF TRUNK DIAMETER'. A note reads '*AS NEEDED TO PROVIDE MINIMUM NECESSARY WORK SPACE. IF LESS THAN 1.5m (5'), THEN ADD BOARDS STRAPPED TO TRUNK.' A smaller illustration to the left shows a tree with a fence around it, labeled '24m (8')' and '1.5m (5')*'. A note below reads 'VARIES'. A line points to a building to the right, labeled 'BUILDING'.]\n\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
