{"level":30,"time":1778543056763,"pid":99088,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QA1JWyhxQa5dvXtBr13KbW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PexAh8C4vXJdRiaQUgZiW3","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Bottom boundary of site near OHE line; areas within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) proposed within 15 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor. Landscape Plan shows mitigation trees 0.1-2 feet from OHE line. Cedar Elm (mature height 40-50 ft) and Live Oak (mature height 40-80 ft) are not listed as utility-compatible exceptions. Plant schedule does not verify UC status against ECM Appendix F.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 measured trees at the bottom boundary 0.1 to 2 feet from the OHE line. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies Cedar Elm and Live Oak as proposed trees; the grouping guidance identifies these as maturing to 40-50+ feet and 40-80 feet respectively.","reasoning":"Trees of this size and species are not listed among the utility-compatible exceptions in the grouping guidance (which notes only trees with mature height ≤20 feet are generally UC, with specific exceptions like Texas Mountain Laurel at 25 feet). Being non-UC, they cannot be placed within 15 feet of distribution conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The 0.1-2 foot distances are clearly within the 15-foot prohibition.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Site boundary areas; if transmission facilities are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine whether overhead electric infrastructure is distribution or transmission. Landscape Plan shows generic 'OHE' label without voltage classification or transmission designator. No transmission facility visual indicators (larger structures, taller poles, wider conductor spacing) are evident on landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape Plan shows a line labeled 'OHE' (Overhead Electric) without voltage classification. Vision analysis found no explicit 'transmission' labels, voltage markings (60kV+), or structural characteristics distinguishing transmission infrastructure.","reasoning":"The grouping distinguishes distribution (<60kV) from transmission (≥60kV) facilities with different clearance requirements. Without evidence of transmission classification on the landscape plan, it cannot be determined whether the 50-foot transmission clearances or the 15-foot distribution clearances apply. Applicability of this item is conditional on identifying transmission facilities.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Bottom boundary of site near OHE line; areas within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) proposed within 25 lateral feet of overhead electric distribution conductor. Cedar Elm (10 trees, mature height 40-50 ft) and Live Oak (2 trees, mature height 40-80 ft) shown 0.1-2 feet from OHE line. Plant schedule does not differentiate large trees or list mature heights.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of Sheet 31 shows multiple trees positioned 0.1-2 feet from the OHE line at site boundary. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 specifies Cedar Elm and Live Oak as proposed trees; these species mature to 40-80 feet per standard arboricultural references.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 restricts large trees (≥40 feet) to locations more than 25 feet from distribution conductors. The measured distances of 0.1-2 feet are well within this 25-foot restriction zone. Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both exceeding the 40-foot threshold, violate this requirement.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Site areas; only applicable if transmission facilities are present"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission facilities not identified on landscape plan. Applicability of 50-foot transmission clearance requirement cannot be determined. See EL-2.2.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission facility designations found on landscape plan or electrical plan documents reviewed.","reasoning":"This requirement is conditional on transmission facilities being present or proposed. Since transmission infrastructure cannot be identified, applicability cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":["Transmission easement boundaries; if present on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission easement boundaries not verified on plat or grading plan. Vision check of Sheet 2 (Plat) could not complete analysis. Facts.md identifies transmission easement requirements from Sheet 3 general notes but does not confirm transmission easement location on this specific parcel.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Attempted vision analysis of Sheet 2 (Plat) to identify transmission easement boundaries did not complete. Facts.md references transmission line requirements but does not indicate whether a transmission easement crosses the property.","reasoning":"The requirement depends on whether a transmission easement exists on the site. Sheet 3 Block 13 notes reference transmission easements and structures, suggesting they may exist, but specific easement locations on this parcel were not verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Bottom boundary of site where OHE line runs and poles are presumed to exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead electric utility poles. Landscape Plan shows multiple trees 5-8 feet from the OHE line. While individual poles are not explicitly marked, the presence of the OHE line indicates poles exist to support it. Trees near this line are within the 10-foot pole clearance zone.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 measured trees at 5-8 feet from OHE line running along site boundary. The OHE line marking indicates utility poles exist along this line.","reasoning":"Overhead distribution lines require poles at regular intervals (typically 100-150 feet). The measured distance of 5-8 feet from the OHE line centerline places trees within 10 feet of where utility poles must exist to support the line.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["West of Bldg 2 (transformer pad with tree 21.6 ft away); West of Bldg 8 (transformer pad with tree 6.9 ft away); North of Bldg 1 (transformer pad/pull box with tree within 10 ft); Eastern property line near Bldg 4 (transformer pad with tree within 10 ft)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted electrical equipment. Electrical Design Plan shows multiple transformer pads and pull boxes. Tree canopy symbols are drawn directly overlapping or immediately adjacent to transformer pad locations. Specific measured distances: transformer pad west of Bldg 8 has tree at 6.9 feet; transformer pad east of Bldg 4 has tree within visual 10-foot radius; transformer pad north of Bldg 1 has overlapping tree canopy.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 identified multiple labeled 'Electrical Transformer Pad' and 'Electrical Pull Box' locations with tree canopy symbols (circles) drawn directly overlapping or very close to these equipment locations. Measured distances show 6.9 feet (well within 10 feet) and visual overlaps.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 prohibits trees within 10 feet of pad-mounted equipment. Multiple equipment locations have trees within or overlapping the 10-foot restriction zone.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["West of Bldg 1 (underground electric line with tree at 5.3 feet)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 5 lateral feet of underground electric equipment. Electrical Design Plan shows underground electric line west of Bldg 1 with tree located 5.3 feet away. This is marginally over the 5-foot minimum clearance—essentially at the threshold with minimal buffer.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement specialist calculated distance between underground electric line west of Bldg 1 and adjacent tree at 5.3 feet using the drawing scale (1\" = 20').","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires 5 lateral feet minimum from underground electric equipment. The measured 5.3 feet is technically compliant but with only 0.3 feet margin, representing marginal/borderline compliance rather than clear separation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["West of Bldg 2 (transformer pad with tree at 21.6 feet); other areas within 20 lateral feet of underground equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment lack required root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment). Electrical Design Plan shows transformer pad west of Bldg 2 with tree at 21.6 feet. Landscape Details sheet (Sheet 37) shows standard tree planting and protection details but does not specify root barriers for electric equipment protection.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement identified transformer pad west of Bldg 2 with tree at 21.6 feet from the equipment. Sheet 37 Landscape Details shows tree planting and protection standard details including tree protection fencing (610S-4) and mulching requirements, but no root barrier specifications for electric equipment protection.","reasoning":"Trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment require root barriers per UCM § 1.10.10.4. The measured 21.6-foot distance is within this threshold. Sheet 37 shows comprehensive landscape details but the absence of root barrier specifications (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment) indicates this requirement has not been addressed in the plans.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plans and Plant Schedules (Sheets 31, 35)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant legend and schedule identify all tree species by both common name and botanical name. Shade trees include Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia); ornamental trees include Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) and Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 35 confirmed that the plant schedule tables for both Shade Trees and Ornamental Trees include a column header 'COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME' with complete scientific names listed for all four tree types.","reasoning":"The Reviewer Convention requirement for species identification is satisfied when both common and botanical names are provided. All proposed trees are identified with both designations.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Plant schedule on Landscape Plan sheets"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) not differentiated on plans. Plant schedule lists only minimum planting heights (Cedar Elm: '100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM'; Live Oak: '100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM'), not mature heights. Mature heights of Cedar Elm (40-50 ft) and Live Oak (40-80 ft) are not shown to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 35 plant schedule confirmed that the 'MIN. SPEC.' column lists only minimum planting heights and container specifications, with no mature height data provided for any trees.","reasoning":"To verify compliance with large tree (40+ feet) clearance restrictions, mature heights must be shown on the plans. The absence of mature height notation prevents field verification that large trees meet their respective clearance zones.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan areas where tree clearances are dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree clearances measured from utility pole centerline or structure instead of from outer electric conductor cannot be verified. Landscape Plan shows OHE line and trees but provides no dimension lines indicating how clearances are measured (from conductor, pole centerline, or structure). Measurement methodology is not documented on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 found no dimension lines from trees to the OHE line. No annotations indicate measurement origins (conductor location vs. pole centerline).","reasoning":"The grouping guidance states conductors are offset laterally from poles (approximately 4+ feet from pole center on typical cross arms). Without dimension lines showing measurement origin, compliance with the conductor-based measurement requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan areas where tree clearances are dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree clearances measured from tree canopy instead of from tree trunk (planting location) cannot be verified. Landscape Plan shows no dimension lines from trees to OHE line. Without dimension callouts indicating measurement origins, cannot verify that measurements originate from tree trunk symbol/center rather than canopy edge.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 found no dimension lines from tree symbols to the OHE line with callout notes indicating measurement origin.","reasoning":"Measurements must originate from tree trunk center (planting location), not canopy edge. Without dimension lines and notes showing measurement methodology, this requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan showing tree locations and overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities, but specific species identification of trees near OHE line is not visible on Sheet 31 itself. Trees are labeled as 'M' (Mitigation Trees) on landscape plan; species must be cross-referenced to Sheet 35 plant schedule. This split documentation prevents full clearance verification from a single sheet. No clearance dimensions or notes are provided on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 showed trees and OHE line on the same drawing, but trees are labeled only as 'M' without species identification. Plant schedule is on Sheet 35.","reasoning":"While trees and utilities are shown together graphically, the inability to identify specific species directly on the landscape plan (without cross-referencing another sheet) and the absence of clearance dimensions limit the practical utility of this showing for field verification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas within prohibited clearance zones: bottom boundary (0.1-2 feet from OHE), pad-mounted equipment locations (6.9 feet), and underground equipment locations (5.3 feet)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans propose trees within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. Sheet 3 Blocks 13, 17, and 19 contain generic Austin Energy requirements and owner responsibilities, but no project-specific written approval letter authorizing tree placement within restricted zones is present. Block 13 Note 1 explicitly states 'No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the transmission structure'; no exception approval is documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheet 3 general notes (Blocks 13, 17, 19) and landscape sheets found only generic Austin Energy standard requirements and owner responsibilities. No supplementary documents or correspondence showing explicit written Austin Energy approval for trees within clearance zones were identified.","reasoning":"The grouping guidance states exceptions require 'explicit written approval from Austin Energy.' The site plan notes contain general requirements (owner responsibility to maintain clearances, right to prune/remove trees) but these are not project-specific approvals for the specific tree locations and clearances proposed on this site.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1875,"cache_read_input_tokens":73161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1875},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8aec104c-0835-4d66-891b-4f34e6fe876f","uuid":"419f4232-f43f-4a39-a440-5e302a228ad4"}
