xplicitly shown on the easement plat, and there is no documented analysis confirming whether transformer pads are located within or outside these recorded easements. For the pad that appears to straddle the property boundary, its exact location relative to recorded easements is unclear. Written AE Design approval for any transformers in easements is not provided. An easement conflict analysis is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat shows recorded easements but transformer pad locations are not marked on the easement plat; one pad appears to straddle boundary where easements exist per facts.md.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation of transformer pad locations relative to recorded easements, and without AE Design written approval for any pads in easements, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements and their required widths for Austin Energy accessibility are not depicted or documented on the site plan, plat, or easement exhibit. Easement exhibits or notes showing transformer pad easement locations and widths determined by AE Design are required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and plat review shows no transformer easement symbols, labels, or dimensions; electrical plan notes reference no easement requirements.","reasoning":"Without documented transformer easements and their widths shown on the plans, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to service meters is shown on the electrical plan, but the plan does not contain explicit documentation or labeling confirming that all electrical service routing is 100% on private property. Service routing within the right-of-way or public easements cannot be excluded from the submitted documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows routing from transformers but does not explicitly annotate routing as being on private property only; property boundary lines are shown but service line paths relative to boundaries are not clearly documented.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation or annotation confirming all routing is on private property, compliance cannot be definitively verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan with graphically measured dimensions (ranging approximately 2.9 feet to 14.2 feet in width, and 4.5 to 5.7 feet in depth for various pads), but the electrical plan does not reference Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets, nor does it specify the service type (single-phase or three-phase). AE Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets must be obtained and submitted showing pad dimensions matched to the specified service type and load requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements of transformer pad dimensions from the electrical plan show dimensions ranging 0.9-14.2 feet in one direction and 4.5-5.7 feet in another; no AE Design detail sheet references or pad specifications are documented.","reasoning":"The requirement is to match AE Design-approved specifications; no such approved details are provided with the submittal, therefore the requirement cannot be met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations adjacent to parking and vehicle circulation areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All four transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas and vehicle circulation routes (driveways). Vision analysis confirms no bollards are shown on the electrical plan, site plan, or any construction detail sheets. Bollards are required: 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts per AE Design equipment pad details must be provided, and bollard locations must be shown on the site plan. Bollards must be designed to allow transformer door opening but prevent vehicle impact.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks show all four transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking/circulation areas; review of electrical plan, site plan, and detail sheets reveals no bollard symbols or specifications anywhere in the submitted documents.","reasoning":"The requirement for bollards when pads are within 4 feet of parking/circulation is clearly triggered and not met. No bollards are shown, documented, or detailed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, tanks) are shown to be installed under or over the site's overhead distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility plan review shows overhead distribution lines running along property boundaries and adjacent areas; no buildings or major customer facilities are located directly under these lines.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (customer facilities under overhead lines) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5182,"cache_read_input_tokens":88771,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5182},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3acdde33-d1c5-4711-add7-cfe5036f8982","uuid":"6d076cb4-9f77-4a63-a3ef-8a46b13f67fd"}
