acent to transformer pad locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of site plan and building elevations shows no balconies or overhangs positioned above or adjacent to transformer locations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (balconies or overhangs above/adjacent to pads) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Building facades adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Window/door locations and their elevation relative to grade cannot be definitively determined from the submitted site plan and building sheets. Building cross-sections showing window sill elevations and horizontal clearances are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building locations but does not provide window/door elevations or detailed horizontal clearance dimensions to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Without building elevation drawings or cross-sections showing window/door details and their relationship to transformer pad locations, the 12-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads on west side of site adjacent to concrete sidewalks/pathways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Two transformer pads are located at distances of only 0.9 feet and 0.3 feet from concrete sidewalks/pathways, both falling well short of the 2-foot minimum clearance requirement. Transformer pads must be relocated or sidewalk routing modified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show transformer pads at 0.9 feet and 0.3 feet from concrete pathways/sidewalks shown on the site plan.","reasoning":"Both measured distances are less than the 2-foot minimum required clearance, representing clear non-compliance with this requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairwells are shown adjacent to transformer pad locations on the site plan or floor plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan and building floor plans shows no stairwells positioned adjacent to transformer locations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (stairwells adjacent to pads) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes or emergency stairs serving as fire escapes are shown on the site plan or building elevations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan and site plan show no fire escapes or external emergency stairs adjacent to transformer locations.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (fire escapes present) is not present, therefore this item does not apply to this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements of hot-stick use area clearances are ambiguous due to inconsistent measurement results between vision checks. Directional clearance to access door sides cannot be reliably determined from the plan without AE Design-approved pad orientation and detail sheets. Additional documentation showing transformer pad orientation and access door location is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple vision checks attempting to measure hot-stick clearances produced inconsistent results, with some directional measurements appearing to be less than 10 feet.","reasoning":"Without clear documentation of transformer pad orientation and access door location on the electrical plan, the 10-foot directional clearance requirement cannot be definitively verified. AE Design detail sheets showing pad orientation are needed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations are shown to be within niches, vaults, or enclosed areas with 3+ sides enclosed. All transformers appear to be in open areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of site plan layout shows all transformer pads are located in open parking/drive areas, not within enclosed structures or notched building configurations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (transformer facing confined space) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad east of Building 7, fire lane area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One transformer pad located east of Building 7 (Unit 704) is only 3.1 feet from the proposed fire hydrant located at the southeast curve of the fire lane, falling short of the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement. The transformer pad must be relocated or the fire hydrant position changed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of fire protection plan shows transformer pad at 3.1 feet from fire hydrant symbol on the fire lane.","reasoning":"The measured 3.1 feet is less than the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement, representing clear non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on the landscape plan near transformer locations (12.1 feet and 21.9 feet from one southwest pad). Tree species cannot be definitively cross-referenced from the landscape plan symbols to the tree list to confirm utility-compatible designations per ECM Appendix F. Tree species identification and utility-compatibility verification is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols near transformer locations; tree list (Sheet 32) provides species names but cannot be reliably cross-referenced from the plan drawings to specific symbols.","reasoning":"Without explicit labeling of tree species on the landscape plan or a clear mapping between symbols and the tree list, utility-compatibility cannot be verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southwest transformer pad location near Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrub and groundcover planting is shown immediately adjacent to one transformer pad (southwest location), with only 0.3 feet of clearance. The requirement is minimum 10 lateral feet from the access door side and 5 lateral feet from other sides. Landscaping must be relocated or redesigned to provide required clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement of landscape plan shows shaded groundcover and shrub planting area directly surrounding the southwest transformer pad at 0.3 feet distance.","reasoning":"The measured 0.3 feet clearance is far less than the 5-foot minimum (and 10-foot for access sides), representing clear non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barriers for trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment are not documented on the landscape details or notes. If trees are present within 20 feet of transformer pad locations, root barrier details (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) must be shown on landscape detail sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows trees and shrubs near transformer locations but contains no explicit root barrier details or specifications.","reasoning":"Root barrier requirements cannot be verified from available landscape detail sheets. Detail drawings with root barrier specifications are required.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision review of site plan found no dumpster or trash enclosure symbols or labels.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (dumpsters present) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bicycle parking area north of Building 2"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Short-term bicycle parking spaces shown on the site plan are 11.6 feet from the nearest transformer pad, exceeding the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement shows bicycle parking area 11.6 feet from transformer pad location.","reasoning":"The measured distance exceeds the 5-foot minimum requirement, therefore the requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations are not clearly documented on the submitted site plan. Photometric plan or electrical lighting plan not provided in site plan set. Light pole clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review did not reveal explicitly labeled light pole locations relative to transformer pads.","reasoning":"Without a detailed photometric plan or clear light pole symbols on the site plan, clearance distances cannot be measured.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly labeled on the fire protection plan sheet. Fire lane striping and signage locations are shown, but without transformer pad symbols on this plan, the 15-foot clearance requirement cannot be directly measured. Visual inspection suggests pads may be outside fire lanes, but explicit verification is not possible from submitted documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan shows fire lane layout but does not depict transformer pad locations; transformer pads are marked only on electrical plan.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad symbols on the fire protection plan, direct clearance measurement is not possible. Cross-referencing between sheets is needed but not explicitly documented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements of distances between transformer pads show: 81.2 feet between west pads of Bldgs 1 and 2; 49.8 feet between west pads of Bldgs 2 and 8; 68.1 feet between pad between Bldgs 4-5 and pad east of Bldg 7. All distances exceed the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show transformer pad-to-pad distances ranging from 49.8 to 81.2 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances significantly exceed the 5-foot minimum requirement, therefore the requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements of water line clearances from transformer pads show: 34.8 feet (Pad west of Bldg 1), 11.8 feet (Pad west of Bldg 2), 14.3 feet (Pad east of Bldg 5), 8.6 feet (Pad east of Bldg 6). All measured distances exceed the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show water line clearances ranging from 8.6 to 34.8 feet from transformer pads.","reasoning":"All measured distances exceed the 5-foot minimum requirement, therefore the requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurement of one transformer pad location shows 132.2 feet clearance to wastewater line, which exceeds the 5-foot minimum. However, this measurement represents only one pad location. Comprehensive clearance verification for all transformer pads to all wastewater service lines should be documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurement checked one transformer pad location and found 132.2 feet to the nearest wastewater line.","reasoning":"While one pad exceeds the 5-foot minimum, comprehensive measurements for all pads are incomplete. The measurement shown passes, but full verification requires checking all pad/utility combinations.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are not explicitly marked or labeled on the storm sewer plan sheet. Storm drain lines and infrastructure are shown on the plan, but without transformer pad symbols, the 5-foot horizontal clearance requirement cannot be directly measured from this sheet. Cross-sheet spatial analysis would be required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of storm sewer plan found no transformer pad symbols or labels on that drawing.","reasoning":"Without transformer pad locations shown on the storm sewer plan, clearance distances cannot be directly measured. Spatial comparison across multiple sheets is not documented.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service lines or gas infrastructure are identified on the utility plan or site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of utility plan legend and site plan shows no gas line symbols or references.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (gas service present) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While water and wastewater clearances have been partially verified, horizontal clearance distances from transformer pads to all underground utilities (electric lines, telecommunications, reclaimed water) are not comprehensively documented. A utility clearance analysis table or detailed measurements are required to verify 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance from all utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan shows multiple utility types (W, WW, RW, E, SD) but clearance distances from transformer pad locations are not dimensionally documented.","reasoning":"Without explicit clearance dimensions or analysis table for each utility type relative to each transformer pad, comprehensive compliance verification is not possible from submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad and utility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and utility plan do not contain explicit documentation or analysis confirming that transformer pads and AE underground facilities are not installed over, under, or in conflict with other utility lines, or that customer structures are not installed over AE underground facilities. A utility conflict analysis or certification is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show various utilities but contain no explicit analysis or certification regarding over/under conflicts between transformer pads/AE facilities and other utilities.","reasoning":"Without documented analysis or certification addressing potential utility conflicts, compliance cannot be verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on the electrical plan, and horizontal distances appear adequate (all >15 feet radially). However, the 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance requirement is not explicitly documented or analyzed. Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearance from grade to overhead conductors are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows overhead line routes but does not provide vertical clearance analysis or cross-section drawings.","reasoning":"Without vertical cross-sections or explicit clearance documentation, the sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be directly verified from plan view alone.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision measurements of radial clearances from transformer pads to overhead distribution conductors show: 81.6 feet (Pad west of Bldg 1), 68.3 feet (Pad west of Bldg 2), 67.3 feet (Pad west of Bldg 8), 105.9 feet (Pad between Bldgs 4-5), 42.4 feet (Pad east of Bldg 7). All distances exceed the 15-foot minimum radial clearance requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements show radial distances to overhead distribution conductors ranging from 42.4 to 105.9 feet.","reasoning":"All measured distances significantly exceed the 15-foot minimum radial clearance requirement, therefore the requirement is satisfied.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer locations are shown within niches (transformer accessible from outside but located within building footprint) or enclosed areas. All transformers appear to be in open site areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows all transformer pads located in open parking and drive areas, not within building footprints or enclosed configurations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (transformer in niche or enclosed area) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are shown on the site plan. Niche service applicability is not triggered.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows no niche configurations or installations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (niche service proposed) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas are shown directly above transformer pad locations. Cross-section drawings are not required for this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows no overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed spaces above transformer locations.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (overhead structures above pads) is not present, therefore cross-section drawing requirement does not apply.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical plan does not specify whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type equipment. Grading plan shows drainage flow patterns but does not explicitly analyze drainage direction from transformer pad locations. For oil-filled equipment, liquid flow must be away from buildings. Specification of transformer type and drainage analysis is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan sheet and electrical specifications do not indicate whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type; grading plan shows general drainage but not specific transformer pad drainage direction.","reasoning":"Without confirmation of transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type), the drainage requirement applicability and compliance cannot be determined.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad west of Building 8, near southwest property corner"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vision analysis of the electrical plan shows one transformer pad (west of Building 8) that appears to straddle the western property boundary line, with the pad extending into the sidewalk easement area and potentially into Valley View Road right-of-way. All transformer pads must be located 100% on private property. The transformer pad must be relocated to ensure it is entirely within the property boundary.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check identified five transformer pads total on the electrical plan; one pad near Bldg 8/Unit 703 is drawn directly over the western property boundary line extending into the easement area.","reasoning":"The pad's position straddling the property boundary violates the requirement that all transformers be 100% on private property. This constitutes a clear deficiency.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations, particularly southwest location"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The plat shows multiple easements including drainage, wastewater, electric, and public utility easements. However, transformer pads are not explicitly shown on the easement plat, and there is no documented analysis confirming whether transformer pads are located within or outside these recorded easements. For the pad that appears to straddle the property boundary, its exact location relative to recorded easements is unclear. Written AE Design approval for any transformers in easements is not provided. An easement conflict analysis is required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plat shows recorded easements but transformer pad locations are not marked on the easement plat; one pad appears to straddle boundary where easements exist per facts.md.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation of transformer pad locations relative to recorded easements, and without AE Design written approval for any pads in easements, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements and their required widths for Austin Energy accessibility are not depicted or documented on the site plan, plat, or easement exhibit. Easement exhibits or notes showing transformer pad easement locations and widths determined by AE Design are required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and plat review shows no transformer easement symbols, labels, or dimensions; electrical plan notes reference no easement requirements.","reasoning":"Without documented transformer easements and their widths shown on the plans, the requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to service meters is shown on the electrical plan, but the plan does not contain explicit documentation or labeling confirming that all electrical service routing is 100% on private property. Service routing within the right-of-way or public easements cannot be excluded from the submitted documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows routing from transformers but does not explicitly annotate routing as being on private property only; property boundary lines are shown but service line paths relative to boundaries are not clearly documented.","reasoning":"Without explicit documentation or annotation confirming all routing is on private property, compliance cannot be definitively verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan with graphically measured dimensions (ranging approximately 2.9 feet to 14.2 feet in width, and 4.5 to 5.7 feet in depth for various pads), but the electrical plan does not reference Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets, nor does it specify the service type (single-phase or three-phase). AE Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets must be obtained and submitted showing pad dimensions matched to the specified service type and load requirements.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision measurements of transformer pad dimensions from the electrical plan show dimensions ranging 0.9-14.2 feet in one direction and 4.5-5.7 feet in another; no AE Design detail sheet references or pad specifications are documented.","reasoning":"The requirement is to match AE Design-approved specifications; no such approved details are provided with the submittal, therefore the requirement cannot be met.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations adjacent to parking and vehicle circulation areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All four transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas and vehicle circulation routes (driveways). Vision analysis confirms no bollards are shown on the electrical plan, site plan, or any construction detail sheets. Bollards are required: 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts per AE Design equipment pad details must be provided, and bollard locations must be shown on the site plan. Bollards must be designed to allow transformer door opening but prevent vehicle impact.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks show all four transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking/circulation areas; review of electrical plan, site plan, and detail sheets reveals no bollard symbols or specifications anywhere in the submitted documents.","reasoning":"The requirement for bollards when pads are within 4 feet of parking/circulation is clearly triggered and not met. No bollards are shown, documented, or detailed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, billboards, chimneys, antennas, tanks) are shown to be installed under or over the site's overhead distribution facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility plan review shows overhead distribution lines running along property boundaries and adjacent areas; no buildings or major customer facilities are located directly under these lines.","reasoning":"The applicability condition (customer facilities under overhead lines) is not present, therefore this item does not apply.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"77bc0163-84a2-4531-8992-d8b91b4a5e40"}
